  "raw": {
    "https://waynetalent.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/2/home/requisition/3696?c=waynetalent": {
      "title": "Mentor-In-Residence, Technology Transfer Talent Network",
      "description": "Mentor-In-Residence, Technology Transfer Talent Network | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) Mentor-In-Residence, Technology Transfer Talent Network Detroit, MI, United States | req3696 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 10/14/2026 Back to Search Mentor-In-Residence, Technology Transfer Talent Network Wayne State University is searching for an experienced Mentor-In-Residence, Technology Transfer Talent Network at its Detroit campus location. Wayne State is a premier, public, urban research university located in the heart of Detroit, Michigan where students from all backgrounds are offered a rich, high-quality education. Our deep-rooted commitment to excellence, collaboration, integrity, diversity and inclusion creates exceptional educational opportunities which prepare students for success in a global society. Position Purpose: The Tech Transfer Talent Network (T3N) Mentor-in-Residence (MIR) serves as a senior-level commercialization advisor who accelerates the translation of university innovations into commercially viable products, startup ventures, and licensing opportunities. The MIR works closely with faculty inventors, researchers, students, technology commercialization professionals, entrepreneurs, investors, and industry partners to evaluate early-stage technologies, improve commercialization decision-making, reduce technical and market risk, and advance innovations toward market adoption. As part of the Michigan statewide T3N initiative, the MIR provides entrepreneurial expertise, industry insight, and access to extensive professional networks. The position supports venture creation, startup acceleration, customer discovery, market validation, fundraising readiness, and commercialization strategy development within designated focus areas such as life sciences, physical sciences, automotive and mobility technologies, advanced manufacturing, energy, and digital/software technologies. The MIR plays a critical role in expanding Wayne State’s and Michigan’s innovation ecosystem by helping transform promising research discoveries into high-growth companies, strategic partnerships, and societal impact. Essential Functions : Technology Assessment, Opportunity Evaluation & Commercialization Strategy. Evaluate early-stage technologies for technical feasibility, market opportunity, competitive positioning, intellectual property considerations, and commercialization potential. Provide strategic recommendations to improve technology transfer decision-making and prioritize opportunities with the greatest likelihood of market success. Guide faculty, researchers, and technology commercialization staff through customer discovery, market validation, business model development, and commercialization planning. Startup Formation, Venture Development & Mentorship. Mentor faculty founders, entrepreneurial researchers, students, and startup teams in venture creation and growth. Assist with company formation, commercialization roadmaps, business planning, team development, value proposition refinement, investor readiness, and milestone achievement. Leverage entrepreneurial experience to accelerate startup development and increase venture success rates. Ecosystem Engagement, Investor Connections & Resource Integration. Connect innovators with investors, mentors, industry partners, service providers, accelerators, incubators, and economic development resources. Facilitate introductions that advance commercialization objectives, support strategic partnerships, and expand access to capital and market opportunities. Funding Support, Due Diligence & Commercialization Programs. Assist with the identification, evaluation, and advancement of technologies seeking gap funding, translational research funding, SBIR/STTR support, proof-of-concept funding, and venture investment. Participate in technology diligence, proposal reviews, milestone development, and funding recommendations. Support commercialization programs and innovation initiatives that advance university technologies toward market readiness. Perform other related duties as assigned. Unique Duties: Part-Time position at .49 fte. Minimum Qualifications: Education : Master’s degree Master’s degree from an accredited college or university. Experience : Expert (established subject matter expert, 7+ years’ experience) Master’s degree from an accredited college or university. Experience Expert (established subject matter expert, 7+ years’ experience) Significant experience as an entrepreneur, startup executive, investor, technology commercialization professional, business development executive, or innovation leader. Demonstrated experience evaluating early-stage technologies and advancing them toward commercialization. Experience forming, growing, financing, or advising startup companies. Experience conducting customer discovery, market assessment, product-market fit analysis, and commercialization planning. Experience working with venture capital firms, angel investors, strategic corporate partners, or economic development organizations. Experience working with university technologies, research institutions, or innovation ecosystems preferred. Track record of successfully supporting technology-based venture creation, licensing transactions, or commercialization outcomes. Knowledge, Skills, And Abilities : Strong knowledge of technology commercialization, venture development, startup formation, and innovation ecosystems. Ability to assess technical innovations and identify commercial opportunities across multiple industry sectors. Knowledge of intellectual property, licensing, market validation, customer discovery, and fundraising processes. Understanding of early-stage company financing, investor expectations, and venture growth strategies. Ability to mentor and advise faculty, researchers, entrepreneurs, and startup leadership teams. Strong strategic planning, business analysis, and opportunity assessment skills. Excellent relationship-building and networking abilities with investors, industry partners, and entrepreneurial stakeholders. Strong communication, presentation, facilitation, and report-writing skills. Ability to work collaboratively across universities, disciplines, and stakeholder groups. Demonstrated ability to influence without direct authority and navigate complex innovation environments. Knowledge of Michigan's innovation, entrepreneurship, and economic development ecosystem preferred. School/College/Division: The Division of Research & Innovation Primary Department: H0905 - VP Research Employment Type: Regular Employee Job type: Fractional Time Job category: Staff/Administrative Funding/Salary Information: Compensation type: Hourly Wage Hourly Rate: To be determined Working Conditions: Normal Office Environment. Job Openings: Number of openings: 1 Reposted position: No Background check requirements: University policy requires certain persons who are offered employment to undergo a background check, including a criminal history check, before starting work. If you are offered employment, the university will inform you if a background check is required. Apply Now Share Save Job Wayne State University provides equal employment opportunities to all employees and applicants for employment without regard to race, color, sex, national origin, religion, age, sexual orientation, familial status, marital status, height, weight, disability, veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by applicable law.  The university welcomes applications from persons with disabilities and veterans.  Wayne State is an equal opportunity employer. Equal Opportunity Employer including persons with disabilities and veterans Wayne State University Human Resources * 5700 Cass Avenue * Suite 3638 AAB Detroit, MI * 48202"
    },
    "https://waynetalent.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/2/home/requisition/3691?c=waynetalent": {
      "title": "Manager, Scholarships and Awards",
      "description": "Manager, Scholarships and Awards | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) Manager, Scholarships and Awards Detroit, MI, United States | req3691 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 10/13/2026 Back to Search Manager, Scholarships and Awards Wayne State University is searching for an experienced Manager, Scholarships and Awards at its Detroit campus location. Wayne State is a premier, public, urban research university located in the heart of Detroit, Michigan where students from all backgrounds are offered a rich, high-quality education. Our deep-rooted commitment to excellence, collaboration, integrity, diversity and inclusion creates exceptional educational opportunities which prepare students for success in a global society. Essential functions (job duties): Job\nPurpose As a member of the management team, the Manager of Scholarships and\nAwards will develop, monitor and report on fund balance and expenditures for\nvarious institutionally funded and private scholarship programs. Responsible\nfor coordinated effort and collaboration across multiple units within the office\nand campus community. Oversee and manage Scholarship\nAward Management System (SAMS) as well as support colleges and departments with\ndepartmental award administration. Assists the Associate Director and Sr.\nDirector in facilitating the development, budgeting, and\ninformation-sharing regarding University scholarships.  Serves as the University’s initial contact\nfor matters concerning scholarships. Work activities\ndemand exceptional quality service to students, departments, local, state and\nfederal agencies as well as ensuring program requirements are met. Essential\nFunctions (Essential\nfunctions are the primary duties/major job responsibilities that an employee\nmust be able to perform, with or without reasonable accommodation. The\nessential functions are listed in order of importance.) Demonstrate administrative capability as a financial aid administrator by ensuring practices, policies, and procedures are in compliance with Federal, State, and institutional requirements. Must maintain a thorough working knowledge of financial aid rules and regulations. Assist with the development of financial aid awarding plans, policies, and communications to keep WSU competitive in recruitment and retention of students. Develop detailed statistical analyses and reports outlining fiscal and operational activities; Provide time sensitive data to Associate Director and Senior Director. Monitor and forecast fund balances; monitor and respond to student eligibility compliance requirements for various award programs. Maintain thorough and accurate records and reports to ensure proper change protocols are maintained and practices meet compliance requirements. Assist with training employees as needed to access the university scholarship platform for scholarship selection. Participates in developing software and programs to support and enhance the administration of various scholarship programs. Supervise professional staff. Serve as a functional or project leader for various department or division initiatives; Participate in internal/external audit reviews. Provide written responses and updates to policy changes. Update and reconcile student accounts to reflect eligible award amounts. Must demonstrate working knowledge of federal financial aid awarding rules. Perform internal review and audit of work completed. Represent the department head at various meetings. Perform\nother related duties as assigned. Qualifications: Education Bachelor's degree Bachelor's degree from an\naccredited college or university or an equivalent combination of education\nand/or experience. Experience     \n \n \n \n \n Intermediate (3 to 4 years job-related experience) Demonstrated working\nexperience in higher education, Successful candidate for this position should\nreflect the successful performance in a large, highly complex and fast paced\nenvironment. Knowledge,\nSkills and Abilities COMMUNICATION SKILLS: Interpersonal skills,\nresolving conflicts, promoting cooperation, administering contracts, and\nproviding outstanding customer service. Ability to create written reports and\ndeliver oral presentations. TECHNICAL KNOWLEDGE: Ability to serve as an\nadministrator for scholarship website and online web portals. INTERPERSONAL SKILLS: Effective interpersonal and\ncustomer service skills. Ability to handle pressure situations. Ability to\nexercise professional judgment when financial aid program guidelines do not\nseem to adequately address a specific situation is also essential SUPERVISORY SKILLS: Ability to delegate work, set\nclear direction and manage workflow. Skill and experience in mentoring and\ncoaching of personnel. Ability to train, develop, assess, and offer feedback to\nstaff members. Skill in development of teamwork among staff members. ANALYTICAL SKILLS: Ability to compare, contrast and\nquality check work with a keen attention to detail. Strong analytical skills\nincluding critical thinking and problem-solving skills.  Must be able to forecast resource needs and\nproject processing deliverables. COMPUTER SKILLS: Proficient in the use of Banner and\nMicrosoft Office tools including Excel. Project Management/SMARTSHEETS,\nSalesforce, or other CRM systems.  Statistical\nanalysis including SPSS. Cognos report writer. School/College/Division: H92 - VP Student Affairs Primary department: H9247 - Student Financial Aid (H9247) Employment type: Regular Employee Job type: Full Time Job category: Staff/Administrative Funding/salary information: Compensation type: Annual Salary Hourly rate: Salary minimum: TBD Salary hire maximum: TBD Working conditions: Office environment Job openings: Number of openings: 1 Reposted position: No Reposted reason: None (New Requisition) Prior posting/requisition number: Background check requirements: University policy requires certain persons who are offered employment to undergo a background check, including a criminal history check, before starting work. If you are offered employment, the university will inform you if a background check is required. Apply Now Share Save Job Wayne State University provides equal employment opportunities to all employees and applicants for employment without regard to race, color, sex, national origin, religion, age, sexual orientation, familial status, marital status, height, weight, disability, veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by applicable law.  The university welcomes applications from persons with disabilities and veterans.  Wayne State is an equal opportunity employer. Equal Opportunity Employer including persons with disabilities and veterans Wayne State University Human Resources * 5700 Cass Avenue * Suite 3638 AAB Detroit, MI * 48202"
    },
    "https://waynetalent.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/2/home/requisition/3674?c=waynetalent": {
      "title": "Talent Management Coordinator",
      "description": "Talent Management Coordinator | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) Talent Management Coordinator Detroit, MI, United States | req3674 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 10/13/2026 Back to Search Talent Management Coordinator Wayne State University is searching for an experienced Talent Management Coordinator at its Detroit campus location. Wayne State is a premier, public, urban research university located in the heart of Detroit, Michigan where students from all backgrounds are offered a rich, high-quality education. Our deep-rooted commitment to excellence, collaboration, integrity, diversity and inclusion creates exceptional educational opportunities which prepare students for success in a global society. Essential functions (job duties): JOB PURPOSE This position is responsible for partnering with unit leadership and the Client Services Director to create and enact a talent management plan.   This position reports directly to the Client Services Director and partners with Central HR to execute the talent management program for assigned units. ESSENTIAL FUNCTIONS Partner with unit leadership and the HR Consultant/Client Services Director to develop sourcing plan complete with advertisements, e-postings, etc.  Post and maintain posting of job to Online Hiring system and other job boards. Gather job requirements, create job postings, ensure testing requirements are met, interview, and refer applicants for all non-academic positions e.g., clerical, technical, administrative and management for assigned schools, colleges and divisions. Interpret University policies and contractual agreements related to posting, hiring, staffing and placement. Screen and analyze the information provided on a prospective employee's application form.  Conduct first round screening of applicants.  Conduct first round interviews if applicable. Perform background checks and reference checks, i.e., criminal background, degree verification, reference checks, etc. to gain adequate information on which to base a selection decision. Make job offers and prepare letters of offer.  Coordinate successful unit integration of each new employee, including I-9 verification, health insurance and employment-related forms. Participate in orientation of new employees as needed. Act as liaison with area employment agencies, advertising agencies, temporary agencies to ensure timely staffing of approved positions. Provide input into the development of hiring processes and candidate assessment methodologies and tools for a variety of position levels. Actively participate in the implementation of enhancing the employment brand by leveraging social media to increase Wayne State University's presence in social media (i.e., Twitter, Facebook, LinkedIn). Provide input and feedback on onboarding program and assist in efforts to streamline and enhance orientation and onboarding processes. Assist in the tracking of talent management metrics and other measures to evaluate the effectiveness of sourcing strategies, associated advertising dollars and candidate resource data and reports. Complete weekly report on employment activity.  Compile additional statistical reports on activities as needed. As directed, support career-related events relative to assigned S/C/D. Conduct exit interviews. Perform related work as assigned. WORK CONTEXT Job Reports to: Director. Leadership Accountability: Implements operating plans. Customer Accountability: Interfaces with customers inside the S/C/D. Freedom to Act: Subject to general input from supervisor. Qualifications: MINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS Education: Bachelor's degree. Additional Education Information: Bachelor's degree preferred in Human Resources management, labor or industrial relations, business administration or public administration. Experience: Specialist. Additional Experience Information: At least (3) years related employment/recruiting experience.  Experience working in a union organization preferred. Experience in a higher education institution preferred. Knowledge, Skills and Abilities TECHNICAL KNOWLEDGE - Expected to possess specialized technical know-how in a one or more human resource functions, e.g., employment selection and recruitment. CUSTOMER SERVICE - Responds to customer needs and practices follow-up to ensure customer needs are met. COMMUNICATIONS - Excellent oral and written communications.   Skilled at working with customers at all levels. INTERPERSONAL SKILLS - Effective interpersonal and customer service skills. Must possess ability to build and maintain effective relationships with customers.  Must demonstrate and possess a high level of professional integrity, ethics and confidentiality. TECHNOLOGY - Proficient in the use of Human Resources Business Information Systems (i.e. HRIS, Applicant Tracking, Electronic I-9 Management, etc.) and Microsoft Office tools. ORGANIZATIONAL SKILLS - Excellent ability to independently establish priorities to meet deadlines, work procedures and make decisions.  Ability to apply basic business practices to improve operations. School/College/Division: H49 - Human Resources Primary department: H4901 - HR Client Services Employment type: Regular Employee Job type: Full Time Job category: Staff/Administrative Funding/salary information: Compensation type: Annual Salary Salary hire maximum: Commensurate with experience Job openings: Number of openings: 1 Reposted position: No Background check requirements: University policy requires certain persons who are offered employment to undergo a background check, including a criminal history check, before starting work. If you are offered employment, the university will inform you if a background check is required. Apply Now Share Save Job Wayne State University provides equal employment opportunities to all employees and applicants for employment without regard to race, color, sex, national origin, religion, age, sexual orientation, familial status, marital status, height, weight, disability, veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by applicable law.  The university welcomes applications from persons with disabilities and veterans.  Wayne State is an equal opportunity employer. Equal Opportunity Employer including persons with disabilities and veterans Wayne State University Human Resources * 5700 Cass Avenue * Suite 3638 AAB Detroit, MI * 48202"
    },
    "https://waynetalent.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/2/home/requisition/3689?c=waynetalent": {
      "title": "Research Associate, Basic Sciences - Department of Oncology",
      "description": "Research Associate, Basic Sciences - Department of Oncology | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) Research Associate, Basic Sciences - Department of Oncology Detroit, MI, United States | req3689 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 10/13/2026 Back to Search Research Associate, Basic Sciences - Department of Oncology Wayne State University is searching for an experienced Research Associate, Basic Sciences - Department of Oncology at its Detroit campus location. Wayne State is a premier, public, urban research university located in the heart of Detroit, Michigan where students from all backgrounds are offered a rich, high-quality education. Our deep-rooted commitment to excellence, collaboration, integrity, diversity and inclusion creates exceptional educational opportunities which prepare students for success in a global society. Essential functions (job duties): Design\n  and perform laboratory-based scientific techniques and experiments. Implement\n  or partake in the implementation of research objectives, ensuring compliance\n  with all legal, regulatory and protocol guidelines. Assist staff with\n  experiments /research protocols as required. Communicate with Principal\n  Investigator and Postdoctoral scholars/fellows on the status of research.\n  Assist the Principal Investigator with intra- and extra-mural grant\n  applications, including, but not limited to, participating in performing the\n  research for grant preparation and submissions, and contributing a summary of\n  \"preliminary data\" with charts and/or tables. Responsibilities may\n  also include coordinating correspondence with applicants and grantees,\n  acknowledging receipts of proposals, and maintaining a system to track\n  proposals. Collect and log laboratory\n  results and/or survey data. Proofread and edit research data and documents to\n  ensure accuracy. Evaluate and perform data analysis using graphs, charts, or\n  tables. Write/edit/proofread scientific manuscripts and other documents for\n  publication. Fact-check research documents to ensure accuracy. Prepare\n  research results for professional, scientific, and academic conferences. Summarize\n  and organize data results for submittal to academic and scholarly,\n  peer-reviewed journals. Maintain the laboratory work areas including\n  routine maintenance on laboratory equipment as required. Order and organize\n  required research supplies and records. Maintain cleanliness and organization\n  of workstation. Perform\n  other related duties as assigned. Unique duties: Qualifications: Education: Bachelor's degree ­Bachelor’s degree from an accredited college or university in a related field of study, preferred. ­Requires advanced knowledge, predominantly intellectual in character, in a field of science or learning acquired by a prolonged course of specialized intellectual instruction. Experience: Intermediate (3 to 4 years job-related experience). ­Experience in performing basic research techniques, preferred. Knowledge, Skills and Abilities: Ability to accurately follow research protocols and work independently as required. ­Ability to analyze, summarize, and interpret research findings and data in reports and spreadsheets and communicate results. ­Knowledge of scientific integrity principles. ­Experience in cell, molecular, biological, and biochemical techniques, including cell culture and maintenance of cells in vitro. ­Excellent time management and organizational skills. ­Excellent interpersonal and communication skills and demonstrated ability to work with others in a collaborative environment. ­Experience using Microsoft Office Suite software. Preferred qualifications: School/College/Division: H06 - School of Medicine Primary department: H0632 - Oncology Employment type: Regular Employee Job type: Full Time Job category: Research Funding/salary information: Compensation type: Annual Salary Working conditions: Typical work environment may include a laboratory and/ or office environment. May require working non-standard business hours including evenings and weekends. May be required to travel to scientific conferences. Job openings: Number of openings: 1 Reposted position: No Reposted reason: None (New Requisition) Prior posting/requisition number: Background check requirements: University policy requires certain persons who are offered employment to undergo a background check, including a criminal history check, before starting work. If you are offered employment, the university will inform you if a background check is required. Apply Now Share Save Job Wayne State University provides equal employment opportunities to all employees and applicants for employment without regard to race, color, sex, national origin, religion, age, sexual orientation, familial status, marital status, height, weight, disability, veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by applicable law.  The university welcomes applications from persons with disabilities and veterans.  Wayne State is an equal opportunity employer. Equal Opportunity Employer including persons with disabilities and veterans Wayne State University Human Resources * 5700 Cass Avenue * Suite 3638 AAB Detroit, MI * 48202"
    },
    "https://waynetalent.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/2/home/requisition/3688?c=waynetalent": {
      "title": "Research Assistant, Basic Sciences, - Department of Oncology",
      "description": "Research Assistant, Basic Sciences, - Department of Oncology | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) Research Assistant, Basic Sciences, - Department of Oncology Detroit, MI, United States | req3688 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 10/13/2026 Back to Search Research Assistant, Basic Sciences, - Department of Oncology Wayne State University is searching for an experienced Research Assistant, Basic Sciences, - Department of Oncology at its Detroit campus location. Wayne State is a premier, public, urban research university located in the heart of Detroit, Michigan where students from all backgrounds are offered a rich, high-quality education. Our deep-rooted commitment to excellence, collaboration, integrity, diversity and inclusion creates exceptional educational opportunities which prepare students for success in a global society. Essential functions (job duties): Perform laboratory-based\n  scientific techniques. Assist in designing and performing experiments. Participate\n  in implementing research objectives, ensuring compliance with all legal,\n  regulatory and protocol guidelines. Communicate with Principal Investigator\n  and Postdoctoral scholars/fellows on the status of research. Collect and\n  log laboratory results and/or survey data. Evaluate and perform data analysis\n  using graphs, charts, or tables to highlight the key points of the research\n  results collected in accordance with the research protocols as stipulated. Proofread and edit research data and\n  documents to ensure accuracy. Assist Principal Investigator with\n  writing methods and summarizing/organizing data to be used in preparing and\n  presenting presentations for professional, scientific, and academic\n  conferences, and submittal to academic and scholarly peer-reviewed journals. Maintain\n  the laboratory work areas, including routine maintenance on laboratory equipment as required. Order\n  and organize required research supplies and records. Maintain cleanliness and\n  organization of workstation. Perform\n  other related duties as assigned. Unique duties: Qualifications: Education: Bachelor's degree Bachelor’s degree in a related field of study, preferred. Requires advanced knowledge predominantly intellectual in character in a field of science or learning acquired by a prolonged course of specialized intellectual instruction. Experience: Entry level (less that a year of job-related experience) Experience performing basic research techniques or interacting with human subjects, preferred. Knowledge, Skills and Abilities: Ability to work independently.  Ability to analyze, summarize and interpret research findings and data in reports and spreadsheets and communicate results. Knowledge of scientific integrity principles. Excellent time management and organization skills.  Excellent interpersonal and communication skills and demonstrated ability to work with others in a collaborative environment.  Microsoft office software skills. Preferred qualifications: School/College/Division: H06 - School of Medicine Primary department: H0632 - Oncology Employment type: Regular Employee Job type: Full Time Job category: Research Funding/salary information: Compensation type: Annual Salary Working conditions: Typical work environment may include a laboratory and/ or office environment. May require working non-standard business hours\nincluding evenings and weekends. May be required to travel to scientific conferences. Job openings: Number of openings: 1 Reposted position: No Reposted reason: None (New Requisition) Prior posting/requisition number: Background check requirements: University policy requires certain persons who are offered employment to undergo a background check, including a criminal history check, before starting work. If you are offered employment, the university will inform you if a background check is required. Apply Now Share Save Job Wayne State University provides equal employment opportunities to all employees and applicants for employment without regard to race, color, sex, national origin, religion, age, sexual orientation, familial status, marital status, height, weight, disability, veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by applicable law.  The university welcomes applications from persons with disabilities and veterans.  Wayne State is an equal opportunity employer. Equal Opportunity Employer including persons with disabilities and veterans Wayne State University Human Resources * 5700 Cass Avenue * Suite 3638 AAB Detroit, MI * 48202"
