    "https://waynetalent.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/2/home/requisition/3660?c=waynetalent": {
      "title": "Marketing Project Manager",
      "description": "Marketing Project Manager | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) Marketing Project Manager Detroit, MI, United States | req3660 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 10/1/2026 Back to Search Marketing Project Manager Wayne State University is searching for an experienced Marketing Project Manager at its Detroit campus location. Wayne State is a premier, public, urban research university located in the heart of Detroit, Michigan where students from all backgrounds are offered a rich, high-quality education. Our deep-rooted commitment to excellence, collaboration, integrity, diversity and inclusion creates exceptional educational opportunities which prepare students for success in a global society. Essential functions (job duties): Job Purpose The Marketing Project Manager oversees, optimizes and manages marketing projects from inception to completion, ensuring they meet their objectives in alignment with the university’s communications and marketing plan, and are delivered on time, within scope, and budget. This role involves developing detailed project plans, coordinating with cross-functional teams inside University Communications and Marketing and beyond, and tracking project performance using appropriate metrics and tools. The Marketing Project Manager serves as the lead communications and marketing contact for campus partners, responsible for integrating marketing activities and support within the office. Essential Functions Develop detailed project plans, including creative briefs, scope, timelines, budgets, approvals, and resource allocation, to ensure successful execution of marketing initiatives. Champions actionable results, alignment, and accountability to achieve marketing goals. Communicates and meets regularly with assigned divisions, schools and colleges, or other entities to ensure awareness and alignment of in-progress and upcoming communications and marketing priorities, gather feedback, obtain approvals and adjust work as needed to stay on track. Track industry trends, prepare market and targeting assessments and monitor university initiatives to inform marketing and partner engagement strategies. Brings creative solutions to bear on marketing challenges and opportunities. Coordinate with cross-functional teams, including creative, social media, web, public relations and others to ensure project components are progressing as planned. Coordinates student engagement in communications and marketing activities. Perform other related duties as assigned. WORK CONTEXT Job Reports to: Director. Leadership Accountability: Develops strategic plans and interprets policy. Organizational Accountability: Manages work group within a sub-unit of a department. Financial Accountability: Monitors expenditures. Customer Accountability: Interfaces with customers outside the S/C/D. Freedom to Act: Subject to general input from supervisor. Qualifications: MINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS Education Bachelor's degree in Marketing, Business Administration or related field. Graduation from an accredited college or university or an equivalent combination of education and/or experience. Experience Specialist (minimum 5 years of job-related experience). Knowledge, Skills and Abilities Deep understanding of marketing strategies, channels, branding, customer behavior, creative brief development, budgeting and content creation. Proven project management skills, efficiently managing deadlines and prioritizing tasks to ensure timely project delivery. Proficient in project management tools. Build strong relationships with university partners and guide the creation and implementation of an integrated marketing and communications plan. Strong problem solving and strategic thinking abilities. Exceptional interpersonal, leadership and communication skills to influence and lead across all organizational levels. Outstanding organization and attention to detail. School/College/Division: H87 - Marketing and Communications Primary department: H8711 - VP Marketing & Communications Employment type: Regular Employee Job type: Full Time Job category: Staff/Administrative Funding/salary information: Compensation type: Annual Salary Salary hire maximum: $77,000 Working conditions: Normal office environment. Job openings: Number of openings: 1 Reposted position: No Background check requirements: University policy requires certain persons who are offered employment to undergo a background check, including a criminal history check, before starting work. If you are offered employment, the university will inform you if a background check is required. Apply Now Share Save Job Wayne State University provides equal employment opportunities to all employees and applicants for employment without regard to race, color, sex, national origin, religion, age, sexual orientation, familial status, marital status, height, weight, disability, veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by applicable law.  The university welcomes applications from persons with disabilities and veterans.  Wayne State is an equal opportunity employer. Equal Opportunity Employer including persons with disabilities and veterans Wayne State University Human Resources * 5700 Cass Avenue * Suite 3638 AAB Detroit, MI * 48202"
