    "https://waynetalent.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/2/home/requisition/3659?c=waynetalent": {
      "title": "Student Success Project Manager",
      "description": "Student Success Project Manager | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) Student Success Project Manager Detroit, MI, United States | req3659 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 9/29/2026 Back to Search Student Success Project Manager Wayne State University is searching for an experienced Student Success Project Manager at its Detroit campus location. Wayne State is a premier, public, urban research university located in the heart of Detroit, Michigan where students from all backgrounds are offered a rich, high-quality education. Our deep-rooted commitment to excellence, collaboration, integrity, diversity and inclusion creates exceptional educational opportunities which prepare students for success in a global society. Essential functions (job duties): Job Purpose The Student Success Project Manager plans,\nmanages, and tracks projects and initiatives across multiple student success\nunits. This role designs and maintains transparency of strategic initiatives in\nalignment with the priorities of the university’s broader retention and\ncompletion goals. In addition, the Student Success Project Manager is\nresponsible for partnering with leaders of past initiatives that have advanced\nstudent persistence at Wayne State University to publish project charters and\nformal reports for the student success project repository. Using\npredictive analytics along with institutional dashboards and data assets, this\nposition assesses the academic performance needs of students, with particular\nattention to historically underrepresented and niche populations. This\nposition reports to the Director, Student Success Operational Strategy. Essential Functions (Essential functions are the primary duties/major job\nresponsibilities that an employee must be able to perform, with or without\nreasonable accommodation. The essential functions are listed in order of\nimportance.) Develop reports for student success outcome measures, KPIs, and\nother metrics to ensure attainment of student success objectives. Lead planning, logistics, and outcome analysis for multiple teams\nof the Student Success Collaborative. Increase meaningful collaboration between the Office of Student\nSuccess Operational Strategy and campus partners to drive progress toward student\nretention and completion goals. Effectively leverage student success systems and platforms to analyze,\ntrack, and report on student progress. Manage workflow of ad hoc projects supporting multiple student\nsuccess units. Perform\nother related duties as assigned. Qualifications: Education Bachelor's degree Bachelor’s degree in Education, Instructional Design, Business or related field or equivalent combination of education and relevant experience required. Project management certification, preferred. Experience Intermediate (3 to 4 years job-related experience) Minimum 3 years of experience in higher education in relevant areas: student success, student affairs, data analytics, academic advising, or similar education and experience. Experience with project management software (Asana), knowledge of business practices and operations. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Clear verbal and written abilities, with effective interpersonal and customer service skills. Ability to work independently and as part of a larger team. Ability to compare, contrast and quality check work with a keen attention to detail. Strong analytical skills including critical thinking and problem-solving skills. Proficient with standard office tools (word processing, spreadsheets, presentation creation), research abilities to find relevant materials using online search tools, and database management systems. Proficient in using technology to develop, implement, track, and analyze programs designed to maximize outreach efforts using student information systems. Demonstrated ability to aggregate and analyze data to evaluate outcomes towards set performance goals. Experience with database query and table design. School/College/Division: H92 - VP Student Affairs Primary department: H9206 - Student Retention (H9206) Employment type: Regular Employee Job type: Full Time Job category: Staff/Administrative Funding/salary information: Compensation type: Annual Salary Hourly rate: Salary minimum: TBD Salary hire maximum: TBD Working conditions: Office environment Job openings: Number of openings: 1 Reposted position: No Reposted reason: None (New Requisition) Prior posting/requisition number: Background check requirements: University policy requires certain persons who are offered employment to undergo a background check, including a criminal history check, before starting work. If you are offered employment, the university will inform you if a background check is required. Apply Now Share Save Job Wayne State University provides equal employment opportunities to all employees and applicants for employment without regard to race, color, sex, national origin, religion, age, sexual orientation, familial status, marital status, height, weight, disability, veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by applicable law.  The university welcomes applications from persons with disabilities and veterans.  Wayne State is an equal opportunity employer. Equal Opportunity Employer including persons with disabilities and veterans Wayne State University Human Resources * 5700 Cass Avenue * Suite 3638 AAB Detroit, MI * 48202"
