    "https://waynetalent.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/2/home/requisition/3617?c=waynetalent": {
      "title": "Single Site Coordinator, C2 Pipeline - College of Nursing",
      "description": "Single Site Coordinator, C2 Pipeline - College of Nursing | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) Single Site Coordinator, C2 Pipeline - College of Nursing Detroit, MI, United States | req3617 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 9/15/2026 Back to Search Single Site Coordinator, C2 Pipeline - College of Nursing Wayne State University is searching for an experienced Single Site Coordinator, C2 Pipeline - College of Nursing at its Detroit campus location. Wayne State is a premier, public, urban research university located in the heart of Detroit, Michigan where students from all backgrounds are offered a rich, high-quality education. Our deep-rooted commitment to excellence, collaboration, integrity, diversity and inclusion creates exceptional educational opportunities which prepare students for success in a global society. Essential functions (job duties): Responsible for implementing school age educational activities at one assigned location outlined in the 21st CCLC grant.  Coordinate activities that include academic learning experiences, field trips and site-based liaison among program staff, school staff, community partners, students, and parents. Maintain efficient and safe learning environment for a quality, educationally focused after-school program at assigned location. Ensure that a plan and curriculum is implemented for assigned site for at least 32 weeks during the school year, and for a minimum of 6 weeks of site- based summer camps at assigned site. Design Curriculum that follow the project model and include site-based activities and special events/field trips. Support HR processes for site staff at each assigned location, including the hiring, payroll, and evaluation of all assigned staff. Participate in development, planning and evaluation of C2 Pipeline Programs, under the direction of the Associate Project Director. Attend meetings with teaching and administrative staff at each assigned staff, including both 1-on-1 meetings and building wide staff meetings. Ensure assigned site compliance with: Out-of-School Time Standards and Michigan Department of Education/MiLEAP’s on-site review monitoring expectations, Department of Health and Human Services Daycare Licensing Guidelines, Center for Youth Program Quality- Youth Program Quality Assessment (YPQA) as well as any collaborated compliance negotiated with the local host school district. Perform other related duties as assigned. Unique duties: Qualifications: Education: Bachelor's degree - Bachelor's degree or equivalent combination of education and experience approved by LARA licensing qualifications. Experience: Experienced (minimum 2 years of job-related experience) - Two years’ experience managing a K-12 after school enrichment program or in lieu of a bachelor’s degree. - Five years’ experience in an education setting and/or five years working in an urban 21st CCLC learning program. - Experience training and supervising staff is required - Experience in the planning, implementation and supervision of after school programming - Experience in the development and implementation of new or innovative programs is preferred - Experience with MDE 21st CCLC required evaluation and systems, with include EZ Reports and YPQA. - Knowledge of K-12 curriculum and learning objectives and knowledge of 21st CCLC afterschool enrichment programs in an urban setting acquired through the completion of a bachelor’s degree and Knowledge, Skills and Abilities: - Supervisory Skills: Strong mentoring and coaching skills. Ability to train staff and develop subordinate's skills. Ability to foster teamwork among staff members. Proven ability to manage and train a diverse staff including outside contractors. - Interpersonal Skills: Ability to establish and maintain effective working relationships and deal effectively with others. Ability to handle a variety of circumstances with tact and diplomacy and in a confidential manner. Ability to work collaboratively and effectively with all school systems personnel is required. - Organizational Skills: Ability to prioritize and plan work activities and monitor workflow. Ability to effectively coordinate program employees and participants to achieve desired results. - Business Acumen: Understands the objectives and mission of the grant; looks for ways to improve processes and quality. Preferred qualifications: School/College/Division: H15 - College of Nursing Primary department: H1501 - Dean's Office Nursing Employment type: Regular Employee Job type: Full Time Job category: Staff/Administrative Funding/salary information: Compensation type: Annual Salary Working conditions: Normal office environment.\nLocal travel and some evenings/weekends required. Job openings: Number of openings: 1 Reposted position: No Reposted reason: None (New Requisition) Prior posting/requisition number: Background check requirements: University policy requires certain persons who are offered employment to undergo a background check, including a criminal history check, before starting work. If you are offered employment, the university will inform you if a background check is required. Equal employment opportunity statement: Wayne State University provides equal employment opportunities to all employees and applicants for employment without regard to race, color, sex, national origin, religion, age, sexual orientation, familial status, marital status, height, weight, disability, veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by applicable law. The university welcomes applications from persons with disabilities and veterans. Wayne State is an equal opportunity employer. Apply Now Share Save Job Wayne State University provides equal employment opportunities to all employees and applicants for employment without regard to race, color, sex, national origin, religion, age, sexual orientation, familial status, marital status, height, weight, disability, veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by applicable law.  The university welcomes applications from persons with disabilities and veterans.  Wayne State is an equal opportunity employer. Equal Opportunity Employer including persons with disabilities and veterans Wayne State University Human Resources * 5700 Cass Avenue * Suite 3638 AAB Detroit, MI * 48202"
    },
    "https://waynetalent.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/2/home/requisition/3616?c=waynetalent": {
      "title": "Assistant / Associate Professor of Educational Leadership and Policy Studies",
      "description": "Assistant / Associate Professor of Educational Leadership and Policy Studies | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) Assistant / Associate Professor of Educational Leadership and Policy Studies Detroit, MI, United States | req3616 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 9/14/2026 Back to Search Assistant / Associate Professor of Educational Leadership and Policy Studies Wayne State University is searching for an experienced Assistant / Associate Professor of Educational Leadership and Policy Studies at its Detroit campus location. Wayne State is a premier, public, urban research university located in the heart of Detroit, Michigan where students from all backgrounds are offered a rich, high-quality education. Our deep-rooted commitment to excellence, collaboration, integrity, diversity and inclusion creates exceptional educational opportunities which prepare students for success in a global society. Position Purpose : The College of Education at Wayne State University is pleased to invite applications for a tenure-track/tenured Assistant/Associate Professor of Educational Leadership and Policy Studies . Preference is to hire at the Associate Professor level, with tenure, but we will consider candidates at the advanced tenure-track Assistant Professor level. Salary and rank for position are commensurate with qualifications and experience. Start Date: August 18, 2027 The Program: Educational Leadership and Policy Studies is a program within the Division of Administrative & Organizational Studies in the College of Education. We serve graduate students in our Master’s of Education in Administration, Education Specialist, Ed.D., and Ph.D. programs. We serve a diverse student body, and nearly half of our students identify as Black. Most of our students work full-time in local K-12 schools or the university community while earning their degrees. Program faculty lead and participate in the research center Detroit Partnership for Education Equity & Research ( Detroit PEER ). The Wayne State University Community: Wayne State University is classified as a \"doctoral university: very high research activity\" by the Carnegie Classification of Institutions of Higher Education. We are located in Midtown Detroit, the city center and one of the country's fastest-growing neighborhoods, which welcomes more than 2.5 million visitors annually. Here, you'll find 200 acres of green space, walking paths and state-of-the-art facilities surrounded by renowned cultural institutions and industry-leading employers. Minimum Qualifications : Earned doctorate in educational leadership, educational policy, or a related field. Educational Policy or Leadership Focus : We seek a scholar whose research addresses educational policy or leadership, broadly defined (e.g., administrative responsibilities such as teacher and staff recruitment and retention; school improvement; leadership and organizational theories, school or district policy implementation; student outcomes, etc.). Scholarly Productivity : We seek a seasoned scholar who has published extensively in educational administration and/or policy academic journals and has a clear, compelling research agenda that has significance for the field (e.g., publication in influential journals and/or media outlets, state- or national-level speaking engagements, community-based programming with notable individual/group impact, external research funding, etc.). Doctoral Advising : Applicants must have an interest in and capacity to begin advising EdD and PhD students in the first year of appointment. Embody Program Values : Important review criteria include evidence of a commitment to working with individuals from diverse backgrounds; commitment to excellence in teaching and advising; and eagerness to embody the program theme: To prepare educational leaders who are reflective, innovative professionals who will affirm and demonstrate their commitment to equitable and just education. Application Process: All applicants must use the WSU Online Hiring System at http://jobs.wayne.edu , referring to Position #3616 . Electronic applications must include a cover letter; curriculum vita (CV); names and contact information for at least three references; and 2 to 3 representative publications/papers for review. The search tee will begin reviewing applications on October 1, 2026 and continue until the position is filled. Applicants whose materials are submitted by October 31, 2026, will guarantee full review. Inquiries about the position may be directed to the chair of the search committee: Dr. Sarah Winchell Lenhoff, sarah.lenhoff@wayne.edu Professor of Educational Leadership and Policy Studies Director, Detroit Partnership for Education Equity & Research Inquires about the application portal or logistics may be directed to: Lei Juan Stewart-Walker, ab2628@wayne.edu . Preferred Qualifications: Externally\nFunded Research: We\nare excited about applicants who have demonstrated the ability to raise\nexternal funds to support their research. Partnered\nResearch: Our\nprogram faculty are involved in active research partnerships with local school\ndistricts and community-based organizations. We would prefer applicants who have\nexperience or interest in conducting partnered, community-based, or policy or\npractice-relevant research. School/College/Division: H02 - College of Education Primary department: H0252 - Administrative & Organizational Stu Employment Type: Regular Employee Job type: Full Time Job category: Academic/Faculty Funding/Salary Information: Compensation type: Annual Salary Hourly rate: Salary minimum: Salary hire maximum: Working Conditions: Normal faculty environment. Job openings: Number of openings: 1 Reposted position: No Background check requirements: University policy requires certain persons who are offered employment to undergo a background check, including a criminal history check, before starting work. If you are offered employment, the university will inform you if a background check is required. Apply Now Share Save Job Wayne State University provides equal employment opportunities to all employees and applicants for employment without regard to race, color, sex, national origin, religion, age, sexual orientation, familial status, marital status, height, weight, disability, veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by applicable law.  The university welcomes applications from persons with disabilities and veterans.  Wayne State is an equal opportunity employer. Equal Opportunity Employer including persons with disabilities and veterans Wayne State University Human Resources * 5700 Cass Avenue * Suite 3638 AAB Detroit, MI * 48202"
    },
    "https://waynetalent.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/2/home/requisition/3614?c=waynetalent": {
      "title": "Exercise & Sport Science, Assistant / Associate Professor, Teaching",
      "description": "Exercise & Sport Science, Assistant / Associate Professor, Teaching | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) Exercise & Sport Science, Assistant / Associate Professor, Teaching Detroit, MI, United States | req3614 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 9/11/2026 Back to Search Exercise & Sport Science, Assistant / Associate Professor, Teaching Wayne State University is searching for an experienced Exercise & Sport Science, Assistant / Associate Professor, Teaching at its Detroit campus location. Wayne State is a premier, public, urban research university located in the heart of Detroit, Michigan where students from all backgrounds are offered a rich, high-quality education. Our deep-rooted commitment to excellence, collaboration, integrity, diversity and inclusion creates exceptional educational opportunities which prepare students for success in a global society. Position Purpose: Rank: Assistant/Associate Professor – Teaching (non-tenure track) with a specialization in Exercise and Sport Science. Program Area: B.S. in Exercise and Sport Science & M.S. in Exercise and Sport Science. Term: Full-time, 9-month, 2 years The Division of Kinesiology, Health, and Sport Studies in the College of Education at Wayne State University seeks a full-time, 9-month Assistant Professor – Teaching (non-tenure track) with specialization in Exercise and Sport Science to teach courses, advise students, and provide service to the program/division/college/university. Responsibilities: Teach face-to-face, hybrid, and/or online courses in the Exercise and Sport Science undergraduate and graduate programs. Advise undergraduate and graduate students related to coursework, internships, and career preparation. Assist with the WSU Higher Learning Commission (HLC) and Committee on Accreditation for the Exercise Sciences (CoAES) accreditation systems. Coordinate undergraduate-level initiatives and programs (i.e., Honors option, student organization, professional development activities, student success initiatives, etc.). Assist divisional and program faculty and administrators with student recruitment and retention initiatives, program assessment, establishing field/practicum experience sites, and other duties required to meet organizational needs. Participate in service activities that support the Division, College, University, and profession. Minimum Qualifications: Ph.D. degree in Kinesiology, Exercise Science, Exercise Physiology, Sport Performance, Human Performance, or a closely related discipline. Minimum of three years of university teaching experience. Evidence of effective university teaching experience, including face-to-face instruction using best practices in course delivery. Evidence of effective online teaching experience, including course development, instructional design, and online pedagogy. Evidence of effective use of the Canvas or related learning management system. Demonstrated ability to advise undergraduate and graduate students in coursework, internships, and career preparation. Proven ability to interact and collaborate effectively with diverse groups of colleagues and students. Demonstrated effective oral and written communication skills. Preferred Qualifications: Professional certifications such as CSCS, NSCA, ACSM, or other nationally recognized credentials.\n\nEvidence of teaching experience across the sub-disciplines of Exercise and Sport Science.\n\nExperience integrating technology, performance assessment, data analytics, wearable technologies, or applied laboratory experiences into teaching.\n\nExperience working with collegiate, secondary school, professional, fitness and performance organizations, or corporate wellness settings.\n\nEvidence of leadership in collaborative initiatives and program operations. School/College/Division: H10 - Health & Physical Education Primary Department: H1007 - Kinesiology Health & Sports Studies Employment Type: Regular Employee Job type: Full Time Job category: Academic/Faculty Funding/Salary Information: Compensation type: Annual Salary Annual Salary:  To be Determined Working Conditions: Normal faculty environment. Job Openings: Number of openings: 1 Reposted position: No Background check requirements: University policy requires certain persons who are offered employment to undergo a background check, including a criminal history check, before starting work. If you are offered employment, the university will inform you if a background check is required. Apply Now Share Save Job Wayne State University provides equal employment opportunities to all employees and applicants for employment without regard to race, color, sex, national origin, religion, age, sexual orientation, familial status, marital status, height, weight, disability, veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by applicable law.  The university welcomes applications from persons with disabilities and veterans.  Wayne State is an equal opportunity employer. Equal Opportunity Employer including persons with disabilities and veterans Wayne State University Human Resources * 5700 Cass Avenue * Suite 3638 AAB Detroit, MI * 48202"
