    "https://waynetalent.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/2/home/requisition/3584?c=waynetalent": {
      "title": "Academic Services Officer I/II",
      "description": "Academic Services Officer I/II | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) Academic Services Officer I/II Detroit, MI, United States | req3584 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 9/1/2026 Back to Search Academic Services Officer I/II Wayne State University is searching for an experienced Academic Services Officer I/II at its Detroit campus location. Wayne State is a premier, public, urban research university located in the heart of Detroit, Michigan where students from all backgrounds are offered a rich, high-quality education. Our deep-rooted commitment to excellence, collaboration, integrity, diversity and inclusion creates exceptional educational opportunities which prepare students for success in a global society. Essential functions (job duties): Job Purpose: The Colonel Gregory Gadson Office of Military and Veterans Academic Excellence (Gadson OMVAE), in partnership with the University Advising Center (UAC), seeks an Academic Services Officer I/II to join its dedicated team of professionals providing high-quality, student-centered, and culturally responsive support. This position will be primarily housed within Gadson OMVAE and will provide supplemental academic advising, outreach, transition support, and student-success programming for Wayne State University’s veteran and military-connected student population. The successful candidate will also support the daily operations of the Student Veterans Resource Center and serve as a liaison between military-connected students, academic departments, and other University offices. In addition, the position will serve as a member of the UAC’s Pre-Med and Health Science Center (PMHSC), providing academic advising and programming to students pursuing pre-nursing, pre-medical, pre-dental, and pre-physician assistant pathways. The Academic Services Officer I/II will report to the Senior Director of University Advising and will work closely with Gadson OMVAE leadership regarding the position’s military-connected student support responsibilities. Essential Functions: · Support the academic onboarding of Wayne State University’s veteran and military-connected student population. · Provide initial and ongoing supplemental academic advising, outreach, transition support, and student-success programming for veterans and military-connected dependents. · Create a welcoming environment that promotes belonging, engagement, persistence, and academic success. · Coordinate the veteran holistic admissions review process, including application review, consultation, admitted-student tracking, monitoring, and outreach. · Develop and distribute communications, alerts, and programming related to student success, enrollment, scholarships, military-connected benefits, and campus opportunities in coordination with the Gadson OMVAE benefits-certification team. · Build collaborative relationships and serve as a point-of-contact liaison to academic departments and other University offices regarding individual and collective military-connected student needs and concerns. · Support the daily operations, programming, and student engagement activities of the Student Veterans Resource Center. · Assist military-connected students with navigating University policies, academic requirements, and campus resources. · Help students balance academic responsibilities with employment, family, military service, and other life commitments. · Coordinate Primary School Letter documentation for students seeking approval to complete coursework at another institution. · Provide advising and support to students preparing for nursing, medical, dental, and physician assistant programs within the WSU Pre-Med and Health Science Center · Assist students with prerequisite course planning, co-curricular development, patient-care experience requirements, testing, assessments, and the application process for professional programs. · Assist students exploring alternative academic and career pathways, including career changers and students reconsidering their intended professional program. · Participate in WSU Open Houses, admission yield events, orientation programs, and other outreach initiatives supporting Gadson OMVAE and PMHSC priorities. · Support the University Advising Center with New Student Orientation, including early outreach, course scheduling assistance, and advising presentations. · Make appropriate referrals to academic, financial, personal, career, and other student-support offices. · Maintain accurate and detailed advising records in the STARS student advising platform. · Participate in regular advisor training and professional development focused on building and maintaining advising competencies. · Perform other related duties as assigned. Unique duties: Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: · Bachelor’s degree required for Academic Services Officer I. · Master’s degree in counseling, higher education leadership, student affairs, student personnel services, or a related field required for Academic Services Officer II. · Minimum of two years of professional experience in higher education, academic advising, student services, or a related area. · Excellent interpersonal, oral, and written communication skills. · Demonstrated ability to collaborate effectively across academic and administrative units. · Experience working with diverse student populations. · Ability to manage multiple priorities effectively and meet established deadlines. · Experience advocating for student needs, goals, and concerns in support of student persistence, achievement, and success. · Strong commitment to promoting educational access and achievement. · Demonstrated decision-making, organizational, and time-management skills, with strong attention to detail. · Ability to work occasional evening and weekend hours. · Excellent computer skills and the ability to adapt to new software programs, student-information systems, and online resources. Preferred Qualifications: · Experience working with veterans, service members, military-connected dependents, or other nontraditional student populations. · Experience providing academic advising or student-success support in a college or university setting. · Experience with pre-health, pre-nursing, or professional-school advising. · Experience reviewing admission applications or supporting admission and enrollment outreach. · Experience using student-information, advising, case-management, or customer-relationship-management systems. · Knowledge of University policies, student-support services, and referral processes. Preferred qualifications: School/College/Division: Generic Division Primary department: H9244 Employment type: Regular Employee Job type: Full Time Job category: Staff/Administrative Funding/salary information: Compensation type: Annual Salary Hourly rate: Salary minimum: Salary hire maximum: Working conditions: Wayne State University is a premier, public, urban research university located in the heart of Detroit, where students from all backgrounds are offered a rich, high-quality education. Our deep-rooted commitment to excellence, collaboration, integrity, diversity, and inclusion creates exceptional educational opportunities that prepare students for success in a diverse, global society. WSU encourages applications from women, people of color, and other underrepresented groups. WSU is an affirmative action/equal opportunity employer. Job openings: Number of openings: 1 Reposted position: No Reposted reason: None (New Requisition) Prior posting/requisition number: Background check requirements: University policy requires certain persons who are offered employment to undergo a background check, including a criminal history check, before starting work. If you are offered employment, the university will inform you if a background check is required. Apply Now Share Save Job Wayne State University provides equal employment opportunities to all employees and applicants for employment without regard to race, color, sex, national origin, religion, age, sexual orientation, familial status, marital status, height, weight, disability, veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by applicable law.  The university welcomes applications from persons with disabilities and veterans.  Wayne State is an equal opportunity employer. Equal Opportunity Employer including persons with disabilities and veterans Wayne State University Human Resources * 5700 Cass Avenue * Suite 3638 AAB Detroit, MI * 48202"
    },
    "https://waynetalent.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/2/home/requisition/3581?c=waynetalent": {
      "title": "Research Technician",
      "description": "Research Technician | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) Research Technician Detroit, MI, United States | req3581 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 8/26/2026 Back to Search Research Technician Wayne State University is searching for an experienced Research Technician at its Detroit campus location. Wayne State is a premier, public, urban research university located in the heart of Detroit, Michigan where students from all backgrounds are offered a rich, high-quality education. Our deep-rooted commitment to excellence, collaboration, integrity, diversity and inclusion creates exceptional educational opportunities which prepare students for success in a global society. Essential functions (job duties): Position Overview Reporting to the Center for Urban Studies’ Directors, the research technicians will provide operational support for the AmeriCorps Community Training (ACT) initiative and related projects on overdose rescue. Duties and Responsibilities: ● Assist in ensuring that AmeriCorps initiatives meet grant all output requirements (tracking/monitoring program outputs and performance measures, drafting project updates and reports, completing required trainings and certifications, preparing documentation for program files, etc.). ● Assist in grant management activities, including programmatic reports in eGrants and OnCorps. ● Assist in maintaining community naloxone access points, including overseeing data collection, and reporting. ● Become fully knowledgeable about national AmeriCorps requirements, policies, and procedures; and diligently adhere to AmeriCorps guidelines in all aspects of program operations. ● Assist in completing routinized activities and procedures for AmeriCorps: o R ecruit new AmeriCorps service members and meet quarterly enrollment targets (update position postings, proactively identify networks and pathways for promoting the position, circulate recruitment information to key contacts, review applications, conduct interviews, etc.). o Complete enrollment, exit, or other status changes (gathering and organizing required documents, conducting criminal history checks, preparing payroll forms, entering member data into WSU and AmeriCorps/ OnCorps systems, etc.). o Verify that all member records are accurate, complete, and compliant with funder guidelines; maintain file checklists and complete regular file audits to ensure member records are up to date . ● Perform other duties as deemed necessary to support program goals. Unique duties: Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: ● A Bachelor’s degree (or working towards a degree) in the social sciences (including political science, public administration, public health, environmental science, education, geography, psychology, social work, sociology, and/or urban studies) is highly preferred . · Experience working within Detroit neighborhoods or similar communities, and community outreach or promotion is highly desirable. Experience with AmeriCorps programs and policies is highly preferred. Must have experience training, coaching, and supervising groups. · Must have excellent written and verbal communication skills. Ability to provide clear instructions and patient guidance to assist members in completing tasks; comfortable providing constructive feedback. Must be able to perform math necessary to verify member timesheets and service hours. Confidence using spreadsheets to organize and analyze data is highly desirable. Previous experience with online data management and reporting systems used by AmeriCorps ( eGrants and OnCorps ) is highly preferred. Experience with customer relationship management (CRM) software is an advantage. Must be proficient in Microsoft Office (Word, Excel, PowerPoint, etc.) and Google products (Drive, Sheets, Docs, Forms, Calendar, etc.). Must be willing and able to learn new systems and software as needed. Prior professional experience in a public service organization (governmental, university, or nonprofit) is preferred. Must be self-motivated; able to initiate and complete tasks independently, anticipate project needs, and proactively plan and prioritize work activities to meet deadlines. Must demonstrate ability to collaborate, work inclusively as part of a team, and establish positive relationships with people of diverse cultural backgrounds (including team members, prospective service members, community partners, and other stakeholders). Submissions must include a cover letter describing relevant experience, an updated resume and most recent transcript (unofficial) , list of references, and recent writing samples . Preferred qualifications: School/College/Division: Generic Division Primary department: H6614 Employment type: Temporary Employee Job type: Fractional Time Job category: Staff/Administrative Funding/salary information: Compensation type: Hourly Wage Hourly rate: $20-$23 Salary minimum: Salary hire maximum: Working conditions: Job openings: Number of openings: 2 Reposted position: No Reposted reason: None (New Requisition) Prior posting/requisition number: Background check requirements: University policy requires certain persons who are offered employment to undergo a background check, including a criminal history check, before starting work. If you are offered employment, the university will inform you if a background check is required. Apply Now Share Save Job Wayne State University provides equal employment opportunities to all employees and applicants for employment without regard to race, color, sex, national origin, religion, age, sexual orientation, familial status, marital status, height, weight, disability, veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by applicable law.  The university welcomes applications from persons with disabilities and veterans.  Wayne State is an equal opportunity employer. Equal Opportunity Employer including persons with disabilities and veterans Wayne State University Human Resources * 5700 Cass Avenue * Suite 3638 AAB Detroit, MI * 48202"
    },
    "https://waynetalent.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/2/home/requisition/3580?c=waynetalent": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor in American Government and Urban Politics",
      "description": "Assistant Professor in American Government and Urban Politics | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) Assistant Professor in American Government and Urban Politics Detroit, MI, United States | req3580 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 8/26/2026 Back to Search Assistant Professor in American Government and Urban Politics Wayne State University is searching for an experienced Assistant Professor in American Government and Urban Politics at its Detroit campus location. Wayne State is a premier, public, urban research university located in the heart of Detroit, Michigan where students from all backgrounds are offered a rich, high-quality education. Our deep-rooted commitment to excellence, collaboration, integrity, diversity and inclusion creates exceptional educational opportunities which prepare students for success in a global society. Essential functions (job duties): The Department of Political Science at Wayne State University has a full-time (9-month) tenure-track opening at the level of Assistant Professor in American Government and Urban Politics, to begin on or about August 18, 2027. We seek candidates whose scholarship investigates contemporary issues in American and urban politics. A successful candidate will conduct research and teach undergraduate and graduate courses in American government and urban politics. Specifically, applicants will be required to teach courses in American Politics, Urban Politics (including Detroit politics), and African American Politics or Race, Class, and Politics. Special consideration will be given to candidates who can teach courses with community engagement in the Detroit metropolitan area. The standard teaching load is 2:2 (fall/winter semesters). Wayne State University is an urban-serving, premier research university in Detroit, Michigan. WSU is classified by the Carnegie Foundation as a RU/VH (Research University, Very High research activity) institution and serves more than 24,000 students across 370 academic programs. The Department of Political Science offers a BA in political science, a BS in public affairs, a graduate certificate in nonprofit management, an MPA program, and MA/Ph.D. programs in political science. Wayne State University is an equal opportunity employer. Qualifications: Applicants must have earned a Ph.D. in political science, public administration, or a related field by the time of the appointment. Demonstrated potential for excellence in scholarship and teaching is required. Applicants should submit a letter of interest, curriculum vitae, and evidence of teaching effectiveness through the Wayne State University jobs website: https://jobs.wayne.edu. Applicants should arrange to have three letters of reference sent to Dr. Brady Baybeck, Interim Chair, at brady.baybeck@wayne.edu Questions about the position should be directed to Brady Baybeck, Interim Chair, at brady.baybeck@wayne.edu. Review of applications will begin October 1, 2026 and continue until the position is filled. School/College/Division: H12 - College of Liberal Arts & Science Primary department: H0323 - Political Science Employment type: Regular Employee Job type: Full Time Job category: Academic/Faculty Funding/salary information: Compensation type: Annual Salary Working conditions: This position must be filled pursuant to the provisions of a collective bargaining agreement, and as such may be filled by a qualified bargaining unit member, should one apply. Job openings: Number of openings: 1 Background check requirements: University policy requires certain persons who are offered employment to undergo a background check, including a criminal history check, before starting work. If you are offered employment, the university will inform you if a background check is required. Apply Now Share Save Job Wayne State University provides equal employment opportunities to all employees and applicants for employment without regard to race, color, sex, national origin, religion, age, sexual orientation, familial status, marital status, height, weight, disability, veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by applicable law.  The university welcomes applications from persons with disabilities and veterans.  Wayne State is an equal opportunity employer. Equal Opportunity Employer including persons with disabilities and veterans Wayne State University Human Resources * 5700 Cass Avenue * Suite 3638 AAB Detroit, MI * 48202"
