    "https://waynetalent.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/2/home/requisition/3578?c=waynetalent": {
      "title": "HIV Prevention Specialist - Department of Internal Medicine",
      "description": "HIV Prevention Specialist - Department of Internal Medicine | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) HIV Prevention Specialist - Department of Internal Medicine Detroit, MI, United States | req3578 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 8/25/2026 Back to Search HIV Prevention Specialist - Department of Internal Medicine Wayne State University is searching for an experienced HIV Prevention Specialist - Department of Internal Medicine at its Detroit campus location. Wayne State is a premier, public, urban research university located in the heart of Detroit, Michigan where students from all backgrounds are offered a rich, high-quality education. Our deep-rooted commitment to excellence, collaboration, integrity, diversity and inclusion creates exceptional educational opportunities which prepare students for success in a global society. Essential functions (job duties): Job Purpose: Coordinates the grant funded Human Immunodeficiency Virus test site for the Wayne State University Adult Human Immunodeficiency Virus Program under the direction of the Psychosocial Team Leader.  Serves as a patient advocate/non-medical case manager, for the psychosocial team.  Reports to Supervisor. Essential Functions: Serves as a patient advocate/non-medical case manager for the psychosocial team. Enrolls eligible patients and maintains patients in the Ryan White program. Assesses patients for barriers to care such as issues with health insurance, transportation, housing and food insecurity.   In collaboration with other members of the psychosocial team, assesses patients for unmet behavioral health needs.  Directly assists patients with barriers and/or links patients with formal case management within the Wayne State University Human Immunodeficiency Virus Prevention program or at community agencies.  Provides health education counseling and risk reduction strategies to project participants. Documents assessments and advocacy/non-medical case management interventions in the medical record and in the Ryan White reporting system. Serves as key contact/liaison HIV testing and other related activities. Obtains testing approval; coordinates and conducts Human Immunodeficiency Virus finger stick testing. Ensures documentation regarding test clients is complete, ensures that documentation of services is included in the medical record for clinic patients, and enters data on test clients and results into the state reporting system. Links positive test clients and patients with disease intervention specialists for Partner Services.   Prepares counseling, testing and referral supplies, forms, packets and educational materials and coordinates distribution of prevention supplies. Ensures trained Counseling, Testing and Referral staff are educated on new testing procedures and maintains record of staff Counseling, Testing, and Referral certification. Maintains certification in Human Immunodeficiency Virus test counseling and performance point of service testing. Maintains knowledge base regarding insurance access and Ryan White policies and procedures regarding non-medical case management, health education and risk reduction, psychosocial support, insurance access and partner services. Participates in ongoing training in counseling skills and cultural sensitivity provided or arranged by the program. Organizes and participates with community outreach efforts, special events, and other health promotion initiatives. Performs other related duties as assigned. Unique duties: Qualifications: Education: Bachelor's degree Bachelor's degree in public health, psychology, sociology, counseling or related field from an accredited college or university. Two or more years' experience as a test counselor providing Human Immunodeficiency Virus support services to clients may be considered in lieu of a Bachelor's degree. Experience: Experienced (minimum 2 years of job-related experience) Two or more years experience working in a public health or clinical setting coordinating HIV prevention programs and services.  Must obtain state-sponsored Human Immunodeficiency Virus prevention counseling and testing training/certification within 3 months of hire. Knowledge, Skills and Abilities: Can apply effective interpersonal skills to provide service. Can respond effectively to most sensitive inquiries or complaints. Self-Directed and able to make decisions and organize work. Can prioritize and plan work activities. Can adapt for changing conditions. Ability to deal with frequent change, delays, or unexpected events. Ability to facilitate training sessions and prepare project site reviews or audits.  Ability to provide services to gay, lesbian, bisexual and transgender clients. Basic knowledge of Microsoft Office. Preferred qualifications: School/College/Division: H06 - School of Medicine Primary department: H0609 - Internal Medicine Employment type: Regular Employee Job type: Full Time Job category: Staff/Administrative Funding/salary information: Compensation type: Annual Salary Hourly rate: Salary minimum: TBD Salary hire maximum: TBD Working conditions: Travel to off-campus sites as required. Some evening and weekend hours for special events as requested. Job openings: Number of openings: 2 Reposted position: No Reposted reason: None (New Requisition) Prior posting/requisition number: Background check requirements: University policy requires certain persons who are offered employment to undergo a background check, including a criminal history check, before starting work. If you are offered employment, the university will inform you if a background check is required. Apply Now Share Save Job Wayne State University provides equal employment opportunities to all employees and applicants for employment without regard to race, color, sex, national origin, religion, age, sexual orientation, familial status, marital status, height, weight, disability, veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by applicable law.  The university welcomes applications from persons with disabilities and veterans.  Wayne State is an equal opportunity employer. Equal Opportunity Employer including persons with disabilities and veterans Wayne State University Human Resources * 5700 Cass Avenue * Suite 3638 AAB Detroit, MI * 48202"
    },
    "https://waynetalent.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/2/home/requisition/3577?c=waynetalent": {
      "title": "Academic Coordinator - Jacob Scholars Program - College of Nursing",
      "description": "Academic Coordinator - Jacob Scholars Program - College of Nursing | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) Academic Coordinator - Jacob Scholars Program - College of Nursing Detroit, MI, United States | req3577 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 8/25/2026 Back to Search Academic Coordinator - Jacob Scholars Program - College of Nursing Wayne State University is searching for an experienced Academic Coordinator - Jacob Scholars Program - College of Nursing at its Detroit campus location. Wayne State is a premier, public, urban research university located in the heart of Detroit, Michigan where students from all backgrounds are offered a rich, high-quality education. Our deep-rooted commitment to excellence, collaboration, integrity, diversity and inclusion creates exceptional educational opportunities which prepare students for success in a global society. Essential functions (job duties): The Academic Coordinator for the Jacob Scholars Program coordinates academic support, student success, and recruitment activities for undergraduate Jacob Scholars in the Wayne State University College of Nursing. The primary focus of the position is supporting the academic success, retention, and progression of Jacob Scholars through tutoring, Supplemental Instruction, group study, academic monitoring, and early intervention. The Academic Coordinator works collaboratively with faculty, academic advisors, the Academic Success Center, and Jacob Scholars Program leadership to coordinate student support services and monitor program outcomes. The position also supports recruitment and outreach efforts to build a pipeline of prospective students into the Jacob Scholars Program, with approximately 30% of the position dedicated to recruitment activities. Occasional evening and weekend hours may be required for student programming, tutoring, recruitment, and program events. Academic Support and Student Success – Approximately 70% Coordinate year-round academic support services for Jacob Scholars, including tutoring, study groups, Supplemental Instruction, academic skills workshops, and pre-semester preparation activities in collaboration with the Academic Success Center. Recruit, onboard, train, schedule, and supervise peer tutors and student assistants; maintain appropriate hiring , training, scheduling, and employment documentation. Monitor student academic progress and engagement, identify students who may benefit from additional support, and collaborate with faculty, advisors, and program leadership to coordinate early intervention strategies. Collaborate with faculty and the Academic Success Center to ensure tutoring, Supplemental Instruction, and other academic support activities align with course objectives and identified student needs. Coordinate tutoring schedules, student communications, academic support materials, workshops, and other resources designed to promote student success, retention, and progression. Track student participation, academic performance, tutoring utilization , and other program outcomes; prepare reports and use data and student feedback to support continuous program improvement. Maintain accurate and confidential student and program records in accordance with university policies. Support Jacob Scholars Program activities, assessment, events, and special initiatives and collaborate with the Director of Jacob Scholars, College of Nursing faculty and staff, university partners, and foundation stakeholders as needed. Recruitment and Outreach – Approximately 30% Coordinate recruitment and outreach activities for the Jacob Scholars Program, including visits to local high schools, college fairs, information sessions, community events, and other prospective student activities. Promote the Jacob Scholars Program and Wayne State University College of Nursing BSN programs to prospective students and families and provide information about program opportunities, eligibility, academic expectations, and available student support. Develop and maintain relationships with high school counselors, teachers, administrators, and community partners to increase awareness of the Jacob Scholars Program and strengthen the prospective student pipeline. Conduct follow-up outreach with prospective students and collaborate with College of Nursing recruitment, admissions, and advising staff to support students through the recruitment and enrollment process; maintain records and track recruitment activities and outcomes. Unique duties: Qualifications: Bachelor’s degree , Master’s degree preferred One to three years of experience in academic support, tutoring, student success, higher education, advising, recruitment, outreach, or a related area. Strong organizational, interpersonal, written, and verbal communication skills. Ability to work effectively with college students, prospective students, families, faculty, staff, and community partners. Ability to coordinate multiple activities, schedules, and priorities and maintain accurate program records. Ability to collect, track, and report student participation, academic performance, and program outcome data. Ability and willingness to travel locally for high school visits, college fairs, and other recruitment activities. Preferred qualifications: Reliable transportation School/College/Division: H15 - College of Nursing Primary department: H1503 - Nursing Staff, Students, & Other Employment type: Regular Employee Job type: Full Time Job category: Staff/Administrative Funding/salary information: Compensation type: Annual Salary Salary minimum: 45,000 Salary hire maximum: 51,000 Working conditions: Regular work is performed in an academic and student services environment. \n\nLocal travel to high schools, community organizations, college fairs, and recruitment events is required. \n\nOccasional evening and weekend hours may be required for student programming, tutoring, recruitment, and program events. \n\nSalary commensurate with experience and consistent with university guidelines. Wayne State University offers a comprehensive benefits package. Job openings: Number of openings: 1 Reposted position: No Reposted reason: None (New Requisition) Prior posting/requisition number: Background check requirements: University policy requires certain persons who are offered employment to undergo a background check, including a criminal history check, before starting work. If you are offered employment, the university will inform you if a background check is required. Apply Now Share Save Job Wayne State University provides equal employment opportunities to all employees and applicants for employment without regard to race, color, sex, national origin, religion, age, sexual orientation, familial status, marital status, height, weight, disability, veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by applicable law.  The university welcomes applications from persons with disabilities and veterans.  Wayne State is an equal opportunity employer. Equal Opportunity Employer including persons with disabilities and veterans Wayne State University Human Resources * 5700 Cass Avenue * Suite 3638 AAB Detroit, MI * 48202"
    },
    "https://waynetalent.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/2/home/requisition/3576?c=waynetalent": {
      "title": "Associate Director, Research Support Services",
      "description": "Associate Director, Research Support Services | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) Associate Director, Research Support Services Detroit, MI, United States | req3576 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 8/23/2026 Back to Search Associate Director, Research Support Services Wayne State University is searching for an experienced Associate Director, Research Support Services at its Detroit campus location. Wayne State is a premier, public, urban research university located in the heart of Detroit, Michigan where students from all backgrounds are offered a rich, high-quality education. Our deep-rooted commitment to excellence, collaboration, integrity, diversity and inclusion creates exceptional educational opportunities which prepare students for success in a global society. Position Purpose: Manage the day-to-day operations of the Research Support Services team within Sponsored Program Administration. Manage a large volume of financial data in order to maintain accurate financial records for the Expendable Restricted Fund. Ensure compliance with university guidelines and external agency regulations. Essential Functions: Manage the change in labor payroll redistribution and effort reporting processes. Assign work to staff, analyze cost transfers, manage exceptions, and approve financial transactions using the ERP module. Work with university units to ensure timely posting of labor redistributions. Work with Fiscal Operations and Technical Support to resolve suspended transactions. Continual review of process to implement process improvement. Manage the ERP Labor Redistribution Module including testing, implementation of enhancements and troubleshooting system errors. Manage effort reporting process to ensure compliance with federal guidelines. Review and maintain the effort reporting email in-box and answer any questions that may arise. Manage the ERP Effort Reporting Module including testing, implementation of enhancements and troubleshooting system errors. Various fiscal compliance and data integrity functions are as follows: Provide assistance to administrators in interpretation of the federal Uniform Guidance standards and specific sponsoring agencies grant and contract terms. Communicate with external sponsors, investigate, and respond to inquiries and coordinate timely problem resolution. Manage various fiscal year-end activities. Manage chart of account data elements to ensure proper coding of revenue and expenditure transactions. Assist in coordination of the annual single audit. Manage the grant/fund financial closeout process for both cost based and fixed price projects. Ensure that all reconciliation items are paid within the Uniform Guidance and Sponsored Program administration standards. Manage the Cost Share funding process. Ensure that all cost share accounts are funded in the proper fiscal year. Review expenditure transfer requests to ensure compliance with university and agency guidelines and regulations. Keep abreast of federal regulations regarding expenditure transfers and communicate any changes to the university community. Analyze cost transfers for compliance with cost accounting standards. Ensure that required justification is provided, and appropriate documentation is retained for audit purposes. Approve cost transfers as a financial officer. Manage the cash management functions for the restricted funds including the application of wire/cash and cash requests on various federal letters of credit. Ensure compliance with federal cash management standards. Act as the Authorized Financial Official for Federal Letter Credits Financial Reports and Cash Draws. Serve as an Authorized Financial Official for Federal Systems, including National Science Foundation, Housing and Urban Development, US Department of Defense, and others as implemented. Personnel management functions including direct supervision of staff, interviewing, hiring, promotion recommendations, performance appraisals, etc. Analyze and review work completed by the staff, including Federal letters of Credit reports, various financial aid reports, payroll redistribution and close out activities. Prepare status reports on unit activities. Assess workload issues and distribution of assignments. Other duties as assigned. Minimum Qualifications: Education :   Bachelor’s degree Bachelor’s degree from an accredited college or university in Accounting, Finance, or related discipline. Experience : Prior experience in the management of sponsored research funds, preferred. Supervisory experience and/or demonstrated experience functioning in a lead capacity with oversight responsibilities, preferred. Knowledge and experience with the principles and practice of governmental accounting, including Generally Accepted Accounting Principles (GAAP). In depth knowledge of the Federal Uniform Guidance. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities : Planning/Organizing Skills : Prioritizes and plans work activities; adapts for changing conditions; communicates changes and progress. Team Building : Develops subordinates' skills and encourages growth; encourages sense of positive affiliation among staff members. Analytical Skills : Analyze accounting, financial, or other quantitative data; detect errors and discrepancies. Problem-Solving Skills : Identifies and resolves problems in timely manner; gathers and analyzes information skillfully; develop alternative approaches and ideas; solves complex problems. Communication Skills : Strong written and verbal communication skills; strong customer service skills. Computer Skills : Proficient in Microsoft Office applications, ERP Banner system, and Cognos reporting tools. School/College/Division: The Division of Research & Innovation Primary Department: H0912 - Sponsored Program Administration Employment Type: Regular Employee Job type: Full Time Job category: Staff/Administrative Funding/Salary Information: Compensation type: Annual Salary Annual Salary: To be determined Working Conditions: Normal office environment. Job Openings: Number of openings: 1 Reposted position: No Background check requirements: University policy requires certain persons who are offered employment to undergo a background check, including a criminal history check, before starting work. If you are offered employment, the university will inform you if a background check is required. Apply Now Share Save Job Wayne State University provides equal employment opportunities to all employees and applicants for employment without regard to race, color, sex, national origin, religion, age, sexual orientation, familial status, marital status, height, weight, disability, veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by applicable law.  The university welcomes applications from persons with disabilities and veterans.  Wayne State is an equal opportunity employer. Equal Opportunity Employer including persons with disabilities and veterans Wayne State University Human Resources * 5700 Cass Avenue * Suite 3638 AAB Detroit, MI * 48202"
    },
    "https://waynetalent.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/2/home/requisition/3575?c=waynetalent": {
      "title": "Digital Content and Communities Assistant",
      "description": "Digital Content and Communities Assistant | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) Digital Content and Communities Assistant Detroit, MI, United States | req3575 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 8/21/2026 Back to Search Digital Content and Communities Assistant Wayne State University is searching for an experienced Digital Content and Communities Assistant at its Detroit campus location. Wayne State is a premier, public, urban research university located in the heart of Detroit, Michigan where students from all backgrounds are offered a rich, high-quality education. Our deep-rooted commitment to excellence, collaboration, integrity, diversity and inclusion creates exceptional educational opportunities which prepare students for success in a global society. Essential functions (job duties): POSITION PURPOSE Assist\nwith the development of WDET's digital content and communications to\nreach and build relationships with new audiences. Implement strategies to grow\nWDET's online communities and engage members in a way that cultivates loyalty, user creativity and viral energy. ESSENTIALJOB FUNCTIONS Assist with the creation and incorporation of daily content into the WDET website. Collaborate with a network of staff journalists; cultivate relationships with a network of diverse contributors and source out of house\nmaterial for incorporation into daily content streams. Assist in quality assurance of all digital content. Develop brand defining communications across multiple social media, social networking and UGC outlets with niche web communities and blog. Engage and grow a wide, diverse community of listener advocates and foster WDET’s ability to learn and adapt\nthrough perpetual audience and community engagement. Serve in a liaison and resource capacity and remain current with industry developments and trends. Assist\nin the gathering and preparation of data and audience analysis. Perform related duties as assigned. ADDITIONAL COMMENTS Coordinate activities to provide content and increase participation in WDET’s digital channels. Assist with the training and\nmotivation of internal and external contributors. This position reports directly to the Digital Manager. Qualifications: Graduation from an accredited college or university or equivalent combination of education and experience. Major coursework in mass communications, broadcast journalism or related field preferred. Reasonable previous related job experience. Demonstrated experience developing digital/multimedia content through a CMS and in depth understanding of CMS software. Reasonable understanding of HTML and CSS. Proven ability to build and engage in communities through social media. Superior verbal\nand written communication skills and attention to detail. Strong analytical and problem-solving skills, including high level understanding of digital metrics. THIS DESCRIPTION IS INTENDED\nTO INDICATE THE TYPES OF TASKS AND LEVELS OF WORK DIFFICULTY THAT WILL BE\nREQUIRED OF POSITIONS THAT WILL BE GIVEN THIS TITLE AND SHALL NOT BE CONSTRUED\nAS DECLARING WHAT THE SPECIFIC DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES OF ANY PARTICULAR\nPOSITION SHALL BE. IT IS NOT INTENDED\nTO LIMIT OR IN ANY WAY MODIFY THE\nRIGHT OF ANY SUPERVISOR TO ASSIGN, DIRECT, AND CONTROL THE WORK OF EMPLOYEES\nUNDER THEIR SUPERVISION. THE USE OF A\nPARTICULAR EXPRESSION OR ILLUSTRATION DESCRIBING DUTIES SHALL NOT BE HELD TO\nEXCLUDE OTHER DUTIES NOT MENTIONED THAT ARE OF A SIMILAR KIND OR LEVEL OF\nDIFFICULTY. School/College/Division: H72 - WDET Primary department: H8703 - WDET (H8703) Employment type: Regular Employee Job type: Full Time Job category: Staff/Administrative Funding/salary information: Compensation type: Annual Salary Hourly rate: Salary minimum:  $52,812.00 Salary hire maximum: $63,377.00 Working conditions: Office environment Job openings: Number of openings: 1 Reposted position: No Reposted reason: None (New Requisition) Prior posting/requisition number: Background check requirements: University policy requires certain persons who are offered employment to undergo a background check, including a criminal history check, before starting work. If you are offered employment, the university will inform you if a background check is required. Apply Now Share Save Job Wayne State University provides equal employment opportunities to all employees and applicants for employment without regard to race, color, sex, national origin, religion, age, sexual orientation, familial status, marital status, height, weight, disability, veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by applicable law.  The university welcomes applications from persons with disabilities and veterans.  Wayne State is an equal opportunity employer. Equal Opportunity Employer including persons with disabilities and veterans Wayne State University Human Resources * 5700 Cass Avenue * Suite 3638 AAB Detroit, MI * 48202"
    },
    "https://waynetalent.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/2/home/requisition/3572?c=waynetalent": {
      "title": "Site Lead - College of Nursing, C2 Pipeline",
      "description": "Site Lead - College of Nursing, C2 Pipeline | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) Site Lead - College of Nursing, C2 Pipeline Detroit, MI, United States | req3572 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 8/21/2026 Back to Search Site Lead - College of Nursing, C2 Pipeline Wayne State University is searching for an experienced Site Lead - College of Nursing, C2 Pipeline at its Detroit campus location. Wayne State is a premier, public, urban research university located in the heart of Detroit, Michigan where students from all backgrounds are offered a rich, high-quality education. Our deep-rooted commitment to excellence, collaboration, integrity, diversity and inclusion creates exceptional educational opportunities which prepare students for success in a global society. Essential functions (job duties): Responsible for assisting the Multi-Level Site Coordinator in implementing high school educational activities at assigned site. Responsible for coordinating activities that include academic learning experiences, field trips and act as site-based liaison among program staff, school staff, community partners, students, and parents. Program development and implementation, open houses, field trips, special exhibits and any performances. Supervise assigned after-school site. Perform daily program functions such as follow-ups on absent students, via phone calls or letters and document all attempts to contact. Distribution and supervision of meals. Remain with students in the cafeteria at all times. Assist with homework, missing or incomplete day school assignments. Lead tutoring sessions for the C2 Pipeline student group. Teach Essential Enrichment classes as needed. Ensure communication plan between day school site and C2 Pipeline program is being followed. Maintain a cooperative and effective working relationship with school district personnel, students, parents, community partners, etc. Responsible for managing and actively engaging high school student groups. Act as a role model for enrolled C2 Pipeline participants socially and academically. Attend all trainings mandated by Michigan Department of Human Services Bureau of Children and Adult Licensing requirements. Participate in additional training and workshops as designated by the after-school program. Effectively plan for the classes, programs and enrichment. Write and or follow lesson plans that accompany the curriculum. Assist with the Michigan Department of Education and MSU 21 st CCLC surveys, data collection and deadlines. Assist with the David P. Wikart Youth Program Quality Assessment (YPQA), assessments and observations. Perform other related duties as assigned. Unique duties: Qualifications: Education: Associate's degree - Bachelor’s Degree in an educational or youth related field preferred. - In lieu of Bachelor's Degree Department the Health and Human Services Licensing Rules for Child Care Centers Rule 400.8122 will be followed to include; Associates degree in Early Childhood Education or Child Development; Montessori Credential with 480 hours experience in a youth related program; valid CDA with 480 hours experience in a youth related program; high school diploma/GED with 12 semester hours in coursework in Early Childhood Education, Child Development and 960 hours experience in youth related field; high school diploma/GED with a combination of 12 semester hours and/or 18 CEU’s to equal 180 clock hours and/or 18 CEU’s to equal 180 clock hours in Early Childhood Education, Child Development or child-related field and 1,920 hours experience in a youth related field; high school Diploma/GED with a combination of 6 semester hours and/or 9 CEU’s to equal 90 clock hours of coursework in Early Childhood Education, Child Development or child-related field and 3,840 hours experience in a youth related field. - Prior to employment, must pass all background checks required by the Department of Human Services Daycare Licensing Guidelines and Wayne State University employment policies. - Must secure Live Scan fingerprinting, show proof of TB Skin Results from within one year of employment, show proof of any immunizations required by the assigned high school or university, show evidence of Blood-borne Pathogen Training prior to working with students. Experience: Experienced (minimum 2 years of job-related experience) - Experience with “At-Risk” youth preferred. - Experience and knowledge in STEM education preferred. - CPR/First Aid certified or willing to obtain certification prior to working with students. Knowledge, Skills and Abilities: - Demonstrate a mature and professional attitude in dealing with students, parents, school district staff and community partners. - Evidence of organizational, supervisory and the interpersonal skills required to run effective pipeline programing and establish good relationships with students, parents, school district staff and co-workers. Preferred qualifications: School/College/Division: H15 - College of Nursing Primary department: H1510 - Nursing C2 Pipeline Employment type: Regular Employee Job type: Fractional Time Job category: Staff/Administrative Funding/salary information: Compensation type: Hourly Wage Working conditions: There are two different sites we'll be hiring for: Communication & Media Arts and Lincoln.\n\nSome evening and weekend work is required.\n\n12-15 hours/week, 2.5-3 hours per day, Monday through Friday predominantly. \n\nHours dependent on student release times at assigned high school. Job openings: Number of openings: 2 Reposted position: No Reposted reason: None (New Requisition) Prior posting/requisition number: Background check requirements: University policy requires certain persons who are offered employment to undergo a background check, including a criminal history check, before starting work. If you are offered employment, the university will inform you if a background check is required. Apply Now Share Save Job Wayne State University provides equal employment opportunities to all employees and applicants for employment without regard to race, color, sex, national origin, religion, age, sexual orientation, familial status, marital status, height, weight, disability, veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by applicable law.  The university welcomes applications from persons with disabilities and veterans.  Wayne State is an equal opportunity employer. Equal Opportunity Employer including persons with disabilities and veterans Wayne State University Human Resources * 5700 Cass Avenue * Suite 3638 AAB Detroit, MI * 48202"
    },
    "https://waynetalent.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/2/home/requisition/3570?c=waynetalent": {
      "title": "Project Coordinator - Department of Oncology, PSDR",
      "description": "Project Coordinator - Department of Oncology, PSDR | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) Project Coordinator - Department of Oncology, PSDR Detroit, MI, United States | req3570 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 8/20/2026 Back to Search Project Coordinator - Department of Oncology, PSDR Wayne State University is searching for an experienced Project Coordinator - Department of Oncology, PSDR at its Detroit campus location. Wayne State is a premier, public, urban research university located in the heart of Detroit, Michigan where students from all backgrounds are offered a rich, high-quality education. Our deep-rooted commitment to excellence, collaboration, integrity, diversity and inclusion creates exceptional educational opportunities which prepare students for success in a global society. Essential functions (job duties): The Project Coordinator will focus on research for the Population Studies Disparities Research (PDSR) for Education and DEI Initiatives. This role will support the Department of Oncology’s mission to coordinate and integrate research and education across the training and professional continuum with an emphasis on building an inclusive cancer research workforce that serves the community. This position reports to both the Associate Center Director of Education and the Associate Center Director of Diversity, Equity, and Inclusion. In this role, the Project Coordinator will provide crucial support to research efforts of WSU’s National Cancer Institute (NCI) designated comprehensive cancer center. The work accomplished by this position ensures that training programs within WSU are effective in reaching students and junior researchers. Ensure that projects are executed successfully and completed within time frames to meet research objectives including maintaining work plans, task lists, project calendars, and the coordination of complex schedules for various initiatives within the Cancer Research Training and Education Coordination (CRTEC) and Diversity, Equity, and Inclusion (DEI) offices within the Department of Oncology at Wayne State University. Provide support to cancer center leaders in writing research reports and manuscripts, developing presentations, contributing to grant submissions, and creating other materials as needed. Liaison to students and community members as well as other cancer research entities. Serves as link between CRTEC, DEI and other essential initiatives of the cancer center, to assemble effective teams of researchers and subject matter experts that will meet the educational and diversity goals of the department. Use artificial intelligence tools for drafting emails, summarizing notes, and conducting research to enhance efficiency in support of initiatives. Schedule, organize and participate in internal and external meetings as the primary event coordinator: developing agendas; setting itineraries for visiting presenters; overseeing all catering, facilities, and audio-visual logistics; and ensuring detailed documentation of outcomes, including post-meeting surveys. Development and analysis of demographic surveys providing insights that can inform strategic initiatives, policies, and programs to assess and understand the diversity and inclusivity of our workforce and academic community. Perform other related duties as assigned. Unique duties: Coordinate daily operations for CRTEC programs serving participants from middle school through faculty, including calendars, shared communications, deadlines, meetings, and program materials.\n\nManage participant applications, communications, reviewer assignments, mentor matching, onboarding, attendance, rosters, alumni records, certificates, and recognition items.\n\nCoordinate sessions, symposia, site visits, career panels, and advisory meetings, including speakers, transportation, registration, facilities, participant movement, day-of operations, evaluations, attendance reconciliation, and archiving.\n\nProcess financial, procurement, and trainee travel transactions, including payment vouchers, purchasing-card documentation, invoices, vendor registration, honoraria, expense reports, reimbursements, index transfers, and approval routing. Maintain complete financial and audit records.\n\nAdminister program surveys; monitor participation; clean, export, and maintain data; update dashboards; conduct alumni and outcome searches; and prepare descriptive summaries.\n\nMaintain CRTEC files, templates, confidential records, and program archives. Support grant and report submissions, approval routing, partner records, joint-event logistics, and tracking of commitments and deliverables. Qualifications: Education: Bachelor's degree Bachelor’s degree in public health, Health Services Administration, or other health related discipline preferred. Experience: Entry level (less that a year of job-related experience) Knowledge of/experience in grant specific requirements. Basic understanding of community school districts, advisory committees, health care systems and resources. Other demonstrated experience of volunteer/community work. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities: · Strong Project Coordination Skillset: Self-motivated, adaptable, and efficient, able to initiate and complete tasks independently; detailed oriented with strong organizational and multi-tasking skills; works competently with ambiguity, possessing strong problem-resolution skills; flexible and able to support multiple and diverse projects within CRTEC and DEI · Effective Team Member: Works well with others who have diverse backgrounds and experiences, demonstrates a strong capacity to collaborate and work towards a common goal. Comfortable accepting and providing constructive feedback. · Excellent Communication Skills: Ability to present effectively to diverse groups, excellent written and verbal communication skills. Must be confident communicating through virtual channels with team members and others. · Proficient Multilingual Skills: Proficiency in English, Arabic, and Spanish for diverse communication is preferred. · Advanced Capabilities with Microsoft Office Products: Skilled in using office software for research papers, data management and presentation preparation. · Proficient in use of artificial intelligence (AI): Ability to use multiple forms of communications, summarizing documents, research efforts, etc. Preferred qualifications: Master’s degree in a related field or an equivalent combination of education and experience.\n\nOne to two years of program, project, or administrative coordination experience, preferably in an academic, healthcare, research, or nonprofit setting.\n\nExperience coordinating programs or events from planning through execution and closeout.\n\nExperience processing financial, procurement, travel, reimbursement, honorarium, or vendor transactions through an institutional system. Familiarity with Wayne State University systems is preferred.\n\nExperience supporting NIH-funded programs, an NCI-designated cancer center, federally sponsored training grants, K-12 programs, or school-district partnerships.\n\nExperience with program-evaluation data, survey platforms such as Qualtrics, structured data entry, dashboards, and descriptive reporting.\n\nExperience handling confidential records under FERPA, HIPAA, or institutional policy and providing work direction to student employees or interns. School/College/Division: H06 - School of Medicine Primary department: H0632 - Oncology Employment type: Regular Employee Job type: Full Time Job category: Research Funding/salary information: Compensation type: Annual Salary Working conditions: Normal office environment. Job openings: Number of openings: 1 Reposted position: No Reposted reason: None (New Requisition) Prior posting/requisition number: Background check requirements: University policy requires certain persons who are offered employment to undergo a background check, including a criminal history check, before starting work. If you are offered employment, the university will inform you if a background check is required. Equal employment opportunity statement: Wayne State University provides equal employment opportunities (EEO) to all employees and applicants for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, national origin, age, disability or genetics. The university encourages applications from women, people of color and other underrepresented people. Wayne State is an affirmative action/equal opportunity employer. Apply Now Share Save Job Wayne State University provides equal employment opportunities to all employees and applicants for employment without regard to race, color, sex, national origin, religion, age, sexual orientation, familial status, marital status, height, weight, disability, veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by applicable law.  The university welcomes applications from persons with disabilities and veterans.  Wayne State is an equal opportunity employer. Equal Opportunity Employer including persons with disabilities and veterans Wayne State University Human Resources * 5700 Cass Avenue * Suite 3638 AAB Detroit, MI * 48202"
    },
    "https://waynetalent.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/2/home/requisition/3567?c=waynetalent": {
      "title": "Behavioral Health Crisis Provider Training Specialist- School of Social Work",
      "description": "Behavioral Health Crisis Provider Training Specialist- School of Social Work | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) Behavioral Health Crisis Provider Training Specialist- School of Social Work Detroit, MI, United States | req3567 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 8/20/2026 Back to Search Behavioral Health Crisis Provider Training Specialist- School of Social Work Wayne State University is searching for an experienced Behavioral Health Crisis Provider Training Specialist- School of Social Work at its Detroit campus location. Wayne State is a premier, public, urban research university located in the heart of Detroit, Michigan where students from all backgrounds are offered a rich, high-quality education. Our deep-rooted commitment to excellence, collaboration, integrity, diversity and inclusion creates exceptional educational opportunities which prepare students for success in a global society. Essential functions (job duties): The Behavioral Health\nCrisis Provider Training Specialist supports the Behavioral Health Crisis\nProvider Training team in the implementation and ongoing delivery of the\nBehavioral Health Crisis Provider Training Program. This position plays a key\nrole in supporting the statewide expansion of behavioral health crisis response\ntraining throughout Michigan, while also contributing to out-of-state training\ninitiatives and partnerships. Primary responsibilities\ninclude providing technical and programmatic support to participants to promote\nsuccessful progression and completion of the training program, coordinating,\nand facilitating in-person Skills Days training across the state, and assisting\nwith the planning, implementation, and evaluation of training activities. The\nTraining Specialist will also collaborate with instructors, community partners,\nand subject matter experts to ensure high-quality training delivery and support\nadditional team-based initiatives that advance the program's goals. This position is housed\nwithin the Center for Behavioral Health and Justice and is a full-time (100%\nFTE) position that reports to the Behavioral Health Crisis Provider Training\nManager. Assist the Behavioral Health\n  Crisis Provider Training Manager in the planning, coordination, and execution\n  of the Behavioral Health Crisis Provider Training Program. Responsibilities\n  include identifying and coordinating Skills Day training locations, managing\n  communication and logistics for Skills Day participants, instructors, and\n  guest presenters, and serving as an instructor during Skills Day trainings\n  across Michigan. Ensures that all training activities are delivered in\n  compliance with Michigan Department of Health and Human Services (MDHHS)\n  requirements. Assesses and evaluates the content and\neffectiveness of individual training modules and the overall Behavioral Health\nCrisis Provider Training Program. Recommends and implements approved\nenhancements or modifications to program content as directed to support\ncontinuous quality improvement. Contributes to the development of quarterly\nprogram reports by compiling, reviewing, and summarizing training data,\nparticipant outcomes, and other program metrics. Supports the development and expansion of\nbehavioral health crisis response education by collaborating on the design,\nimplementation, and evaluation of new training programs, curricula, and\nlearning opportunities. Works with subject matter experts and community\npartners to identify emerging training needs, develop instructional materials,\npilot new initiatives, and integrate evidence-informed practices into future\nprogram offerings. Collaborate with research\n  assistant to monitor participant progress throughout the Behavioral Health\n  Crisis Provider Training Program and provide timely support to promote\n  successful course completion. Assists with the coordination and facilitation\n  of synchronous training sessions, including participant communication,\n  technical support, attendance tracking, and other activities necessary to\n  ensure an effective learning experience. Perform other related duties\n  as assigned. Qualifications: Education Master's degree ­Master's degree from an accredited college or university with a degree in Social Work, Psychology, Counseling, or a related field of study. Experience Intermediate (3 to 4 years job-related experience) ­Clinical practice in crisis response required. ­Training/Instructor experience preferred. ­Must possess and maintain current licensure in the State of Michigan Licensed Clinical Social Worker (LMSW) or Licensed. Professional Clinical Counselor (LPCC) or State of Michigan Limited Licensed Master Social Worker (LLMSW) or Limited Licensed. Professional Counselor (LLPC), with eligibility to obtain full LMSW or LPC licensure as required by the position. ­Professional experience in academic institutions or a similar professional environment designing and managing training programs. KNOWLEDGE, SKILLS, AND ABILITIES ­Technical Skills: Strong knowledge of Excel and publisher mail merge features. Video editing and graphic design experience preferred. Ability to troubleshoot technical issues during live events. ­Organizational Skills: Ability to prioritize and plan work activities to meet deadlines. Ability to work effectively with established deadlines and pressure. ­Communication Skills: Demonstrated verbal and written communication skills with the ability to manage a variety of relationships with various stakeholders. ­Interpersonal Skills: Abel to deal with frequent change, delays, or unexpected events. Changes approach or method to best fit the situation and reacts well under pressure. ­Financial Skills: Manage expenses and perform bookkeeping duties. ­Professionalism: Must demonstrate and possess a high level of professional integrity, ethics, and confidentiality. Demonstrated expertise in collaborating with external partners, such as state agencies, community organizations, or other research institutions. School/College/Division: H13 - School of Social Work Primary department: H1304 - Behavioral Health & Justice Center Employment type: Regular Employee Job type: Full Time Job category: Staff/Administrative Funding/salary information: Compensation type: Annual Salary Salary minimum: $49,700 Salary hire maximum: $74,500 Working conditions: ­\tFrequent travel is required.\n­\tWork may be performed inside or outside of the school facility with exposure to inclement weather and unpredictable crisis situations. Job openings: Number of openings: 1 Background check requirements: University policy requires certain persons who are offered employment to undergo a background check, including a criminal history check, before starting work. If you are offered employment, the university will inform you if a background check is required. Apply Now Share Save Job Wayne State University provides equal employment opportunities to all employees and applicants for employment without regard to race, color, sex, national origin, religion, age, sexual orientation, familial status, marital status, height, weight, disability, veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by applicable law.  The university welcomes applications from persons with disabilities and veterans.  Wayne State is an equal opportunity employer. Equal Opportunity Employer including persons with disabilities and veterans Wayne State University Human Resources * 5700 Cass Avenue * Suite 3638 AAB Detroit, MI * 48202"
