branding across all digital channels. Essential Functions: Define, develop, and curate engaging content for social media platforms. Collaborates with teams to ensure all content aligns with brand voice/vision/campaign. Coordinate with department’s residency and fellowship programs. Develop and maintain the department website and its related pages; coordinate with all divisions for information, and Department leadership Engage with relevant audiences to build following and increase residents and fellow’s enrollment; monitor and report on social media conversations and trends. Track, report, analyze social media campaigns to assess the effectiveness of campaigns and adjust strategies accordingly. Participate in the training of other communicators on effective use of social media. Perform other related duties as assigned. Unique duties: Qualifications: Education: Bachelor's degree Bachelor's degree in Marketing, New Media, Communications, or a related field Graduation from an accredited college or university or an equivalent combination of education and/or experience. Experience: Intermediate (3 to 4 years job-related experience) Knowledge, Skills and Abilities: Working understanding of social media management and content creation strategies for various social platforms. Knowledge of social media campaign management, assessment and listening tools. Experience in data-driven decision-making. Ability to deliver creative content (text, image, and video) in a proactive and impactful way. Ability to grasp future trends in digital technologies and act proactively. Strong written and verbal communication skills, with the ability to engage diverse audiences. Curious and eager to learn new skills as social trends evolve, ensuring branded content is relevant for each channel. Collaborative and able to work with cross-functional teams to maximize content creation and promotion with various campus partners. Excellent organizational and multitasking abilities, with a strong attention to detail. Preferred qualifications: School/College/Division: H06 - School of Medicine Primary department: H0609 - Internal Medicine Employment type: Regular Employee Job type: Full Time Job category: Staff/Administrative Funding/salary information: Compensation type: Annual Salary Hourly rate: Salary minimum: TBD Salary hire maximum: TBD Working conditions: Job openings: Number of openings: 1 Reposted position: No Reposted reason: None (New Requisition) Prior posting/requisition number: Background check requirements: University policy requires certain persons who are offered employment to undergo a background check, including a criminal history check, before starting work. If you are offered employment, the university will inform you if a background check is required. Apply Now Share Save Job Wayne State University provides equal employment opportunities to all employees and applicants for employment without regard to race, color, sex, national origin, religion, age, sexual orientation, familial status, marital status, height, weight, disability, veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by applicable law.  The university welcomes applications from persons with disabilities and veterans.  Wayne State is an equal opportunity employer. Equal Opportunity Employer including persons with disabilities and veterans Wayne State University Human Resources * 5700 Cass Avenue * Suite 3638 AAB Detroit, MI * 48202"
