    "https://waynetalent.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/2/home/requisition/3557?c=waynetalent": {
      "title": "Program Manager, Upward Bound",
      "description": "Program Manager, Upward Bound | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) Program Manager, Upward Bound Detroit, MI, United States | req3557 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 8/12/2026 Back to Search Program Manager, Upward Bound Wayne State University is searching for an experienced Program Manager, Upward Bound at its Detroit campus location. Wayne State is a premier, public, urban research university located in the heart of Detroit, Michigan where students from all backgrounds are offered a rich, high-quality education. Our deep-rooted commitment to excellence, collaboration, integrity, diversity and inclusion creates exceptional educational opportunities which prepare students for success in a global society. Essential functions (job duties): Job\nPurpose The\nUpward Bound (UB) Program Manager is vital in empowering low-income,\nfirst-generation students to pursue higher education. This role involves\nleading efforts to identify, recruit, and enroll high school students into the\nprogram while providing tailored college preparatory and academic support\nservices to help them succeed. From\nrecruitment to graduation preparation, the UB Program Manager oversees various\nservices designed to meet the students’ individual needs. These services\ninclude guiding participants through intake and assessment, offering academic\nadvising and programming, connecting them to tutoring resources, supporting\nthem in selecting colleges, completing applications, and navigating financial aid\nprocesses like Free Application for Federal Student Aid (FAFSA). In addition to\nmanaging participant services, the Program Manager ensures the daily operation\nof the program by supervising full-time, part-time, and temporary staff. Their\nleadership helps create a supportive and effective environment for high school\nstudents transitioning into postsecondary education. This position reports to\nthe Director, Office of Federal TRIO Programs. Essential\nFunctions Develop, implement, and manage programming for\nthe TRIO Upward Bound Program to enhance the educational success of\nparticipants each year, while ensuring compliance with grant objectives, U.S.\nDepartment of Education regulations, and University policies. Lead the recruitment, hiring, onboarding,\ntraining, supervision, and evaluation of full-time and part-time staff,\nfostering a collaborative team dedicated to developing and delivering an\ninnovative academic and college preparatory curriculum that supports students’ academic\ngrowth and smooth transition into higher education. Establish and maintain partnerships with WSU\nstaff and faculty, target schools, and youth-serving community partners to\nrecruit new students to the program and ensure the success of continuing participants. Prepare and\n  monitor grant budget. Complete annual financial reports. Allocate resources\n  and manage expenditures in accordance with federal, University, and\n  departmental policies, and procedures. Develop and manage organized recordkeeping and\ndata collection systems to track participant eligibility, services provided and\nassess program outcomes. Maintain and update participant files while monitoring\ntheir performance, retention, program completion, postsecondary enrollment, and\nprogress toward college graduation. Prepare and submit the UB grant\nproposal and annual performance reports in accordance with Department of\nEducation guidelines to maintain funding. Perform other related duties as assigned. Qualifications: Education Master's degree Master’s degree from an accredited university in education, education administration, educational leadership, higher education, counseling, social work, human services, or related field. Experience Specialist (minimum 5 years of job-related experience) 5 years of full-time professional experience in student access/success programs. 3+ years of academic and administrative experience. Experience with program management and budget management. Experience designing, managing, or implementing similar programs. Experience working with high school or college students, within a TRIO/EOP Program preferred. Experience with grant proposal writing, management, and reporting preferred. Experience using Blumen, Banner, or other data management systems preferred. Knowledge,\nSkills and Abilities Strong leadership, motivational, programming, and organizational skills. Strong interpersonal, communications, presentation, and information management skills. Knowledge of learning theories, learning styles, educational methods, and demonstrated ability to apply student development theories Demonstrated commitment to serving and preparing underserved participants for academic success and post-secondary enrollment. School/College/Division: Generic Division Primary department: H9212 - Office of Academic Student Affairs (H9212) Employment type: Regular Employee Job type: Full Time Job category: Staff/Administrative Funding/salary information: Compensation type: Annual Salary Hourly rate: Salary minimum: TBD Salary hire maximum: TBD Working conditions: Office environment Job openings: Number of openings: 1 Reposted position: No Reposted reason: None (New Requisition) Prior posting/requisition number: Background check requirements: University policy requires certain persons who are offered employment to undergo a background check, including a criminal history check, before starting work. If you are offered employment, the university will inform you if a background check is required. Apply Now Share Save Job Wayne State University provides equal employment opportunities to all employees and applicants for employment without regard to race, color, sex, national origin, religion, age, sexual orientation, familial status, marital status, height, weight, disability, veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by applicable law.  The university welcomes applications from persons with disabilities and veterans.  Wayne State is an equal opportunity employer. Equal Opportunity Employer including persons with disabilities and veterans Wayne State University Human Resources * 5700 Cass Avenue * Suite 3638 AAB Detroit, MI * 48202"
