    "https://waynetalent.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/2/home/requisition/3701?c=waynetalent": {
      "title": "Michigan Poison & Drug Information Center Program Manager - Dept. Emergency Medicine",
      "description": "Michigan Poison & Drug Information Center Program Manager - Dept. Emergency Medicine | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) Michigan Poison & Drug Information Center Program Manager - Dept. Emergency Medicine Detroit, MI, United States | req3701 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 10/16/2026 Back to Search Michigan Poison & Drug Information Center Program Manager - Dept. Emergency Medicine Wayne State University is searching for an experienced Michigan Poison & Drug Information Center Program Manager - Dept. Emergency Medicine at its Detroit campus location. Wayne State is a premier, public, urban research university located in the heart of Detroit, Michigan where students from all backgrounds are offered a rich, high-quality education. Our deep-rooted commitment to excellence, collaboration, integrity, diversity and inclusion creates exceptional educational opportunities which prepare students for success in a global society. Essential functions (job duties): Job Purpose: The Michigan Poison & Drug Information Center Program Manager organizes the administrative and operational activities that support reliable, continuous Poison Center services. This position works closely with Specialists in Poison Information (SPIs), Certified Specialists in Poison Information (CSPIs), directors, and institutional partners to maintain staffing coverage, coordinate staff support, training logistics, event planning, grant submissions, and philanthropical program support. The Program Manager serves as a central point of contact for operations needs and follows through on priorities established by the directors. Essential Functions: Maintain administrative records of professional licenses, certifications, required training, and renewal dates. Develop, plan, and coordinate quarterly education conferences for the tri-county residencies and other educational conferences as they become available. Spearhead and coordinate logistics and planning of Annual MiPDC Toxicology Symposium, and other similar continuing education offerings for health care professionals in the metro Detroit area and beyond. Identify grant and sponsorship opportunities annually to support Poison Center programs, educational materials, travel, and conference attendance. Build and maintain potential prospect and donor tracking system for hospitals, foundations, businesses, community organizations, and individual supporters, in coordination with the development office. Support directors with program implementation and administrative coordination of service agreements, research data contracts, and other business activities. Track deliverable, approvals, renewals, and reporting deadlines with the appropriate institutional offices. Implement and maintain RingCentral ACE performance metrics and phone reviews. Develop and maintain monthly schedules for SPIs and update as needed. Coordinate leave requests, call offs, traded shifts, vacant shifts, and coverage for meetings or training. Identify coverage gaps, seek qualified coverage, and escalate unresolved shortages and overtime needs to the designated director. Provide on-call support for staff operational issues. Support MiPDC staff during events. Create and maintain tables of staff productivity on a bi-weekly basis by collecting data from various sources. Perform random audits to ensure compliance on benchmarks for insurance, self-introductions, chart documentation, etc. Develop standards to improve efficiency and incorporate Lean principles into our daily practice. Educate staff about documentation guidelines. Coordinate with MiPDC Sr. Director and Medical Director for new applicant screening, application reviews, interviews, job offers, interview logistic coordination and scheduling. Develop and/or maintain orientation checklist and supporting materials. Structure MiPDC SPI on-boarding process. Ensure new employees progress through training during shifts. Manage personnel transactions for assigned staff including hiring, promotions, terminations, disciplinary procedures, and salary adjustments. Provide timely communications to department. Provide education support for SPI’s. Create and maintain compliance modules in Canvas. Ensure annual education and compliance modules are completed by SPI’s. Perform other related duties as assigned. Unique duties: Qualifications: Education: Bachelor's degree Bachelor degree from an accredited college or university in business administration, health care administration, public health, communications, nonprofit management, or a related field. An equivalent combination of education and relevant experience may be considered. Graduate education in business, health care administration, public health, or a related field is preferred but not required. Clinical licensure or SPI certification is not required for this non-clinical position. Experience: Intermediate (3 to 4 years job-related experience) Poison center or 24-hour call center experience preferred. Experience supporting licensed health professionals; conference planning, fundraising, donor stewardship, grant coordination, or academic health system experience preferred. Experience in program coordination or administrative coordination that includes staff scheduling, project or event coordination, financial tracking, or comparable responsibilities in health care, academic, public service, or nonprofit setting. Knowledge, Skills, And Abilities: Technical Knowledge: Ability to interpret and implement policies and procedures (including research administration). Proficient in Microsoft Office (Access, Word, Excel, PowerPoint). Proficiency with scheduling software When2Work. Knowledge of Ring Central phone/chat software. Knowledge of relational databases. Proficiency with office productivity software, spreadsheets, calendars, virtual meeting tools, and administrative databases. Ability to learn workforce scheduling and donor management systems. Interpersonal Skills: Effective interpersonal and customer service skills. Ability to work with a diverse population. Ability to manage within a challenging, academic environment, including dealing with sensitive and confidential information and interpersonal dynamics. Supervisory & Leadership Skills: Ability to delegate and supervise assignments, set clear direction, and manage workflow. Strong mentoring and coaching skills. Ability to foster teamwork among staff and faculty members. Demonstrated ability to manage competing deadlines, resolve scheduling problems, maintain accurate records, communicate professionally, and collaborate with multidisciplinary staff. Provides leadership and training to responsible area(s) regarding financial, budgetary, personnel and administrative matters. Demonstrates strong leadership skills that can influence and motivate individuals and groups to achieve results. Organizational Agility: Demonstrates critical thinking and strategic decision-making skills to establish and accomplish the mission, strategic plans, and goals of the unit. Financial Skills: Ability to develop and analyze budgets for grant project. Provide oversight and management of comprehensive budgets. Demonstrates attention to detail. Preferred qualifications: School/College/Division: H06 - School of Medicine Primary department: H0616 - Emergency Medicine Employment type: Regular Employee Job type: Full Time Job category: Staff/Administrative Funding/salary information: Compensation type: Annual Salary Hourly rate: Salary minimum: TBD Salary hire maximum: TBD Working conditions: Work is primarily performed in an office environment.\nOn-call services are available 24/7 for emergent Operational Center issues. Job openings: Number of openings: 1 Reposted position: No Reposted reason: None (New Requisition) Prior posting/requisition number: Background check requirements: University policy requires certain persons who are offered employment to undergo a background check, including a criminal history check, before starting work. If you are offered employment, the university will inform you if a background check is required. Apply Now Share Save Job Wayne State University provides equal employment opportunities to all employees and applicants for employment without regard to race, color, sex, national origin, religion, age, sexual orientation, familial status, marital status, height, weight, disability, veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by applicable law.  The university welcomes applications from persons with disabilities and veterans.  Wayne State is an equal opportunity employer. Equal Opportunity Employer including persons with disabilities and veterans Wayne State University Human Resources * 5700 Cass Avenue * Suite 3638 AAB Detroit, MI * 48202"
    },
    "https://waynetalent.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/2/home/requisition/3695?c=waynetalent": {
      "title": "Faculty (Clinical)- Rank to be Determined - College of Nursing",
      "description": "Faculty (Clinical)- Rank to be Determined - College of Nursing | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) Faculty (Clinical)- Rank to be Determined - College of Nursing Detroit, MI, United States | req3695 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 10/14/2026 Back to Search Faculty (Clinical)- Rank to be Determined - College of Nursing Wayne State University is searching for an experienced Faculty (Clinical)- Rank to be Determined - College of Nursing at its Detroit campus location. Wayne State is a premier, public, urban research university located in the heart of Detroit, Michigan where students from all backgrounds are offered a rich, high-quality education. Our deep-rooted commitment to excellence, collaboration, integrity, diversity and inclusion creates exceptional educational opportunities which prepare students for success in a global society. Essential functions (job duties): Prepare, teach, and evaluate courses, primarily courses related to one’s area of clinical specialization. Apply teaching strategies appropriate to students’ learning needs. Engage in scholarly activities including, but not limited to, publication of clinical, pedagogical, or research-based papers in journals or books; presentations at local, regional or national/international conferences. Conduct and participate in clinical scholarship, teaching scholarship, or research projects in collaboration with other faculty and students. Serve on faculty committees and task forces. Perform related duties as assigned. Unique duties: Qualifications: Doctorate Degree required. Current Advanced Practice Certification required. Previous teaching experience at the undergraduate level or higher in Nursing using both didactic and clinical methods. Recent clinical practice required. Candidate must present the ability to perform the work required, with a previously established pattern of acceptable attendance and performance. Preferred qualifications: The ideal candidate will have experience in at least one of the following areas: care of the perinatal family or psychiatric/mental health nursing with the ability to teach other Nursing courses (i.e., Medical-Surgical Nursing, Community Health, Population\nHealth, Pediatric Nursing etc.), especially if specialty-area courses are not offered within a given semester. School/College/Division: H15 - College of Nursing Primary department: H1501 - Nursing Faculty, PTF & GTA Employment type: Regular Employee Job type: Full Time Job category: Academic/Faculty Funding/salary information: Compensation type: Annual Salary Working conditions: Job openings: Number of openings: 1 Reposted position: No Reposted reason: None (New Requisition) Prior posting/requisition number: Background check requirements: University policy requires certain persons who are offered employment to undergo a background check, including a criminal history check, before starting work. If you are offered employment, the university will inform you if a background check is required. Apply Now Share Save Job Wayne State University provides equal employment opportunities to all employees and applicants for employment without regard to race, color, sex, national origin, religion, age, sexual orientation, familial status, marital status, height, weight, disability, veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by applicable law.  The university welcomes applications from persons with disabilities and veterans.  Wayne State is an equal opportunity employer. Equal Opportunity Employer including persons with disabilities and veterans Wayne State University Human Resources * 5700 Cass Avenue * Suite 3638 AAB Detroit, MI * 48202"
