    "https://waynetalent.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/2/home/requisition/3714?c=waynetalent": {
      "title": "Lead Teacher, Merrill Palmer Skillman Institute",
      "description": "Lead Teacher, Merrill Palmer Skillman Institute | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) Lead Teacher, Merrill Palmer Skillman Institute Detroit, MI, United States | req3714 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 10/27/2026 Back to Search Lead Teacher, Merrill Palmer Skillman Institute Wayne State University is searching for an experienced Lead Teacher, Merrill Palmer Skillman Institute at its Detroit campus location. Wayne State is a premier, public, urban research university located in the heart of Detroit, Michigan where students from all backgrounds are offered a rich, high-quality education. Our deep-rooted commitment to excellence, collaboration, integrity, diversity and inclusion creates exceptional educational opportunities which prepare students for success in a global society. Position Purpose: The Program Lead Teacher plans and manages a state-funded preschool classroom for four-year-old children, ensuring alignment with Michigan Department of Education (MDE), National Association Accreditation Standards and licensing standards including planning and developing an engaging, age-appropriate and developmentally appropriate early childhood curricula, developing weekly lesson plans, organizing programs based upon knowledge of child development and individual needs of children, supervising classroom staff, coaching and mentoring College of Education early childhood education students during their clinical experience at the Merrill Palmer Skillman Institute Early Childhood Center, as well as work study students and student assistants, recording and maintaining student records, assessing, tracking and documenting children’s progress and achievement using authentic child assessment methods, conducting home visits and parent-teacher conferences. The position reports to the Manager, Early Childhood Center. Essential Functions : Implement developmentally appropriate early childhood curricula with an established number of preschool children at the Merrill Palmer Skillman Institute Early Childhood Center; develop weekly lesson plans, organize programs based upon knowledge of child development and individual needs of children; design and deliver age-appropriate lessons using The Project Approach. Conduct team planning sessions with classroom staff at established intervals to plan, implement and evaluate curriculum and plan strategies for children. Work collaboratively with the teaching team, children, families, researchers, and staff to carry out the Merrill Palmer Skillman Institute Early Childhood Center's mission and philosophy as outlined by the Center Director and Executive Director. Record and maintain student records; assess, track and document children’s progress and achievement using authentic child assessment methods; monitor child growth and collect developmental data using the child assessment tool Teaching Strategies GOLD. Participate in staff development activities and weekly staff meetings. Communicate with families in various formats including individual daily contacts, childcare management software, parent/staff meetings, parent-teacher conferences, and newsletters. Obtain resources for children with developmental needs or delays. Participate in periodic performance reviews and annual evaluation with the center director. Performs all other duties as assigned. Minimum Qualifications: Education : Bachelor’s degree Bachelor's degree from an accredited college or university in Elementary Education with a major in Early Childhood Education required. Valid Michigan Elementary Teaching Certificate with a ZA or ZS Endorsement or a Birth-Kindergarten Teaching Certificate required. Experience : Intermediate (3 to 4 years of job-related experience). Experience working with preschool-aged children. Experience with curriculum development and classroom management in an early childhood education program. Experience using authentic assessments to document children's growth and development. Experience using the Teaching Strategies GOLD child assessment tool. Experience using conflict resolution to promote social problem-solving with young children. Experience with implementing The Project Approach curriculum. Experience with childcare management software (Brightwheel, etc.) preferred. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities : Knowledge of The Project Approach curriculum. Extensive knowledge of early childhood development principles and developmentally appropriate educational practices. Enthusiastic personality that will engage preschool children. Excellent communication and interpersonal skills with children, adults, and staff. Ability to collaborate with support staff, adults, and students in a positive and constructive way. Strong organizational skills. Ability to plan, manage and evaluate curriculum. Proficiency with Microsoft Office Suite or related software as required for recordkeeping, documentation, and communication. School/College/Division: The Division of Research & Innovation Primary Department: H0910 - Merrill Palmer Institute Employment Type: Regular Employee Job type: Full Time Job category: Staff/Administrative Funding/salary information: Compensation type: Annual Salary Annual Salary: To be determined Working Conditions: Preschool Classroom. Prolonged periods of standing and walking throughout the\nclassroom. Sit and stand on the floor throughout the day and bend, kneel or\nsquat to be at eye level with children. Periodically lift up to 40 pounds, including a preschool child. Job Openings: Number of openings: 1 Reposted position: No Background check requirements: University policy requires certain persons who are offered employment to undergo a background check, including a criminal history check, before starting work. If you are offered employment, the university will inform you if a background check is required. Apply Now Share Save Job Wayne State University provides equal employment opportunities to all employees and applicants for employment without regard to race, color, sex, national origin, religion, age, sexual orientation, familial status, marital status, height, weight, disability, veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by applicable law.  The university welcomes applications from persons with disabilities and veterans.  Wayne State is an equal opportunity employer. Equal Opportunity Employer including persons with disabilities and veterans Wayne State University Human Resources * 5700 Cass Avenue * Suite 3638 AAB Detroit, MI * 48202"
    },
    "https://waynetalent.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/2/home/requisition/3427?c=waynetalent": {
      "title": "Research Assistant, Data Management Analytics, Division of Research & Innovation",
      "description": "Research Assistant, Data Management Analytics, Division of Research & Innovation | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) Research Assistant, Data Management Analytics, Division of Research & Innovation Detroit, MI, United States | req3427 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 6/17/2026 Back to Search Research Assistant, Data Management Analytics, Division of Research & Innovation Wayne State University is searching for an experienced Research Assistant, Data Management Analytics, Division of Research & Innovation at its Detroit campus location. Wayne State is a premier, public, urban research university located in the heart of Detroit, Michigan where students from all backgrounds are offered a rich, high-quality education. Our deep-rooted commitment to excellence, collaboration, integrity, diversity and inclusion creates exceptional educational opportunities which prepare students for success in a global society. Position Purpose: The Research Assistant position provides technical and analytic support for biomedical and population health research initiatives involving Google Cloud Platform–based research data workflows, BigQuery SQL (Structured Query Language) analytics, structured research databases, interactive dashboards, and AI-integrated research approaches. Essential Functions : Assist with development and maintenance of cloud-based research data workflows and structured analytics environments using Google Cloud Platform technologies, including BigQuery and Cloud Storage. Assist in preparing, transforming, and organizing large structured and unstructured research datasets for downstream analytics, reporting, and AI-enabled approaches. Support implementation of SQL-based (structured query language) research data pipelines and analytic workflows used in biomedical, clinical, and population health research projects. Assist in the development of interactive research dashboards and visualization tools for research and healthcare data using cloud-based analytic platforms. Support research teams in transitioning analytic and data processing workflows toward reproducible cloud-based environments and internally managed research tools. Assist with development and testing of AI-enabled (Artificial Intelligence) workflows, including computer vision, natural language processing, semantic search, and metadata extraction systems for research approaches. Perform other related duties as assigned. Minimum Qualifications: Education : Master’s degree Discipline : Computer Science/ Data Science/ Biomedical Informatics/ Bioinformatics/ Statistics/ Computational Science/ Related computational discipline. Experience : Experienced (minimum 2 years of job-related experience). Plus, two or more of the following is preferred : Google Cloud Platform SQL (Structured Query Language) and relational databases Python programming Cloud-based analytics workflows Dashboard development AI/ML (Artificial Intelligence/Machine Learning) or data science workflows Biomedical or healthcare research data environments Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities : Working knowledge of SQL (Structured Query Language) and structured database concepts. Experience using Python for analytics, scripting, or data processing workflows. Familiarity with cloud computing platforms, particularly Google Cloud Platform technologies such as BigQuery and Cloud Storage. Familiarity with AI/ML (Artificial Intelligence/Machine Learning), natural language processing, or computer vision workflows preferred. Ability to assist with development of dashboards and interactive analytic tools. Ability to work independently while contributing within collaborative research teams. Strong organizational, communication, and problem-solving skills. Knowledge of research integrity and reproducible research principles. Experience with Git-based workflows or collaborative software development environments preferred. School/College/Division: Division of Research & Innovation Primary Department: H0905 - VP Research Employment Type: Regular Employee Job type: Full Time Job category: Research Funding/salary Information: Compensation type: Annual Salary Annual Salary: To Be Determined Working Conditions: Normal Office Environment. Job Openings: Number of openings: 1 Reposted position: No Background Check Requirements: University policy requires certain persons who are offered employment to undergo a background check, including a criminal history check, before starting work. If you are offered employment, the university will inform you if a background check is required. Apply Now Share Save Job Wayne State University provides equal employment opportunities to all employees and applicants for employment without regard to race, color, sex, national origin, religion, age, sexual orientation, familial status, marital status, height, weight, disability, veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by applicable law.  The university welcomes applications from persons with disabilities and veterans.  Wayne State is an equal opportunity employer. Equal Opportunity Employer including persons with disabilities and veterans Wayne State University Human Resources * 5700 Cass Avenue * Suite 3638 AAB Detroit, MI * 48202"
